[2026-11-27T21:00:33.867Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_42","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n '\"'^#{2,4} '\"' dev/log/issues/207/pulls/208/templates/CI-CD-BEST-PRACTICES.md && cat .github/workflows/workflows.yml && git ls-files '*package*.json' && ls -la /tmp/link-cli-207-npm-ci.log\"","aggregated_output":"5:## Why CI/CD Matters for AI Development\n16:## Recommended CI/CD Templates\n35:## Key CI/CD Principles\n42:### 1. Run Checks Only on Relevant File Changes\n99:#### Commit and ready-for-review checks\n117:#### Select monorepo suites from the workspace graph\n137:### 2. File Size Limits\n171:#### Adopt the limit with a ratchet\n177:### 3. Automated Code Formatting\n196:### 4. Static Analysis & Linting\n213:### 5. Fast-Fail Job Ordering\n239:#### Size jobs and start the longest work first\n245:### 6. Changeset-Based Versioning\n275:### 7. Validate the Actual Merge Result\n299:### 8. Pre-commit Hooks\n311:### 9. Release Automation\n334:### 10. Concurrency Control\n397:#### Preserve a full check when a commit arrives\n409:### 11. Secrets Detection\n417:### 12. Documentation Validation\n433:### 13. Container Images: Native Runners per Architecture\n469:### 14. Lint the Workflows Themselves\n489:### 15. Audit the Dependency Tree\n501:### 16. Prove You Can Publish Before You Build\n532:### 17. Tell a Broken Pipeline from a Changed World\n559:## Quality Enforcement Strategy\n579:## Getting Started\n588:### Add Swift CI to a multi-language repository\n595:## Automatic CI/CD Remediation\n611:### Why the issue is a Bug, and what it leaves out\n619:### Language → Template Mapping\n653:## References\nname: Workflows\n\n# Lints the CI/CD definitions themselves (issue #134). Before this workflow\n# nothing ran actionlint or zizmor, and the workflow policy tests only ran\n# when a C# or Rust path changed, so a defect in docs.yml, wasm.yml or\n# links.yml reached main unchecked. Mirrors workflows.yml of the\n# rust/csharp/js ai-driven-development-pipeline templates.\non:\n  push:\n    branches:\n      - main\n    paths:\n      - '.github/**'\n      - 'js/**'\n      - 'csharp/scripts/**'\n      - 'examples/**'\n      - 'experiments/**'\n      - '.pre-commit-config.yaml'\n  pull_request:\n    types: [opened, synchronize, reopened]\n    paths:\n      - '.github/**'\n      - 'js/**'\n      - 'csharp/scripts/**'\n      - 'examples/**'\n      - 'experiments/**'\n      - '.pre-commit-config.yaml'\n  workflow_dispatch:\n\n# Least-privilege default; these jobs only read the checked-out tree.\npermissions:\n  contents: read\n\n# Provide Git config to actions/checkout itself; checkout runs git init before\n# any workflow step can configure Git, which otherwise prints the\n# default-branch hint into every log.\nenv:\n  GIT_CONFIG_COUNT: '1'\n  GIT_CONFIG_KEY_0: ini…nch\n  GIT_CONFIG_VALUE_0: main\n\njobs:\n  actionlint:\n    name: Lint Workflows\n    runs-on: ubuntu-24.04\n    timeout-minutes: 10\n    concurrency:\n      group: check-${{ github.workflow }}-${{ github.ref }}-actionlint\n      cancel-in-progress: true\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v7\n        with:\n          persist-credentials: false\n\n      # The Docker image bundles shellcheck and pyflakes, so this also lints\n      # every `run:` block. A native actionlint binary without shellcheck on\n      # PATH silently skips the shell checks and exits 0. To reproduce locally:\n      #   docker run --rm -v \"$PWD:[REDACTED]\" -w /repo rhysd/actionlint:1.7.12 -color\n      #\n      # Pinned by digest because a mutable tag of a repository we do not\n      # control is arbitrary code execution (the `'*': hash-pin` policy of\n      # .github/zizmor.yml). Re-resolve when bumping:\n      #   docker pull rhysd/actionlint:<tag> &&\n      #   docker inspect --format='{{index .RepoDigests 0}}' rhysd/actionlint:<tag>\n      - name: Lint workflow files\n        uses: docker://rhysd/actionlint@sha256:b1934ee5f1c509618f2508e6eb47ee0d3520686341fec936f3b79331f9315667 # v1.7.12\n        with:\n          args: -color\n\n  zizmor:\n    name: zizmor\n    runs-on: ubuntu-24.04\n    timeout-minutes: 10\n    concurrency:\n      group: check-${{ github.workflow }}-${{ github.ref }}-zizmor\n      cancel-in-progress: true\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v7\n        with:\n          persist-credentials: false\n\n      # actionlint cannot see workflow security defects: unpinned third-party\n      # actions, checkouts that persist GITHUB_TOKEN in .git/config, or\n      # template injection into `run:` blocks. zizmor covers those.\n      #\n      # Only .github is audited: dev/log keeps verbatim copies of the template\n      # workflows as evidence, and they are not run here.\n      #\n      # The action's wheel lock can lag behind PyPI releases. Verify the\n      # wheel against our own lock and share the install between both audits.\n      - name: Install the locked zizmor wheel\n        run: |\n          python3 -m pip install --require-hashes --only-binary=:all: --no-deps \\\n            --target \"$RUNNER_TEMP/zizmor\" -r .github/scripts/requirements-workflow-audit.txt\n\n      # Emit annotations so findings fail the job without code scanning.\n      - name: Audit workflow files\n        env:\n          GH_TOKEN: ${{ github.token }}\n        run: |\n          \"$RUNNER_TEMP/zizmor/bin/zizmor\" --format github --config .github/zizmor.yml .github\n\n      # The audits that cover container image references (`unpinned-images`\n      # among them) are pedantic-only, so the hash-pin policy is not enforced\n      # against `uses: docker://` by the regular pass above. Narrowing this\n      # pass to high severity and high confidence keeps that enforcement\n      # without the stylistic noise of the pedantic persona.\n      - name: Audit for pedantic-only high-severity findings\n        timeout-minutes: 5\n        run: |\n          \"$RUNNER_TEMP/zizmor/bin/zizmor\" --config .github/zizmor.yml \\\n            --persona pedantic --min-severity high --min-confidence high \\\n            .github\n\n  policy:\n    name: Workflow Policy Tests\n    runs-on: ubuntu-24.04\n    timeout-minutes: 10\n    concurrency:\n      group: check-${{ github.workflow }}-${{ github.ref }}-policy\n      cancel-in-progress: true\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v7\n        with:\n          persist-credentials: false\n\n      - name: Setup Node.js\n        uses: actions/setup-node@v7\n        with:\n          node-version: '26.x'\n\n      - name: Run workflow policy tests\n        run: node --test .github/scripts/*.test.mjs\n\n  languages:\n    name: JavaScript and Python lint and formatting\n    runs-on: ubuntu-24.04\n    timeout-minutes: 10\n    concurrency:\n      group: check-${{ github.workflow }}-${{ github.ref }}-languages\n      cancel-in-progress: true\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v7\n        with:\n          persist-credentials: false\n      - uses: actions/setup-node@v7\n        with:\n          node-version: '26.x'\n          cache: npm\n          cache-dependency-path: js/package-lock.json\n      - uses: actions/setup-python@v7\n        with:\n          python-version: '3.14'\n      - name: Install locked JavaScript tools\n        run: npm ci --prefix js --ignore-scripts\n      - name: Check all maintained JavaScript including JSX and examples\n        run: npm --prefix js run lint\n      - name: Install Python tools\n        run: python -m pip install -r .github/scripts/requirements-quality.txt\n      - name: Check all maintained Python and type-check runtime CI helpers\n        run: python .github/scripts/check-python-quality.py\n\n  pipeline-status:\n    name: Pipeline Status (workflows)\n    needs:\n      - actionlint\n      - zizmor\n      - policy\n      - languages\n    if: ${{ !cancelled() }}\n    runs-on: ubuntu-24.04\n    timeout-minutes: 5\n    concurrency:\n      group: check-${{ github.workflow }}-${{ github.ref }}-pipeline-status\n      cancel-in-progress: true\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v7\n        with:\n          persist-credentials: false\n      - uses: actions/setup-node@v7\n        with:\n          node-version: '26.x'\n      - name: Check every prerequisite\n        working-directory: .\n        env:\n          NEEDS_JSON: ${{ toJSON(needs) }}\n        run: node .github/scripts/pipeline-status.mjs\n.package-registry-manager.json\njs/client/package-lock.json\njs/client/package.json\njs/package-lock.json\njs/package.json\njs/server/package-lock.json\njs/server/package.json\n-rw-r--r-- 1 box box 0 Nov 27 20:59 /tmp/link-cli-207-npm-ci.log\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
