[2026-11-27T21:02:42.655Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_81","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"gh issue view 1528 --repo link-assistant/hive-mind --json body,title,url,comments && gh issue view 1436 --repo link-assistant/hive-mind --json body,title,url --jq '{title,body: (.body | .[0:3500])}'\"","aggregated_output":"{\"body\":\"We should double check our CI/CD logic to not trigger on irrelevant files like `.gitkeep` file example: https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/pull/1527/changes/0e01568591d8c9043f3d6378ba1cf748dc6a3adf\\n\\nSee CI/CD logs for the commit.\\n\\nWe need to download all logs and data related about the issue to this repository, make sure we compile that data to `./docs/case-studies/issue-{id}` folder, and use it to do deep case study analysis (also make sure to search online for additional facts and data), in which we will reconstruct timeline/sequence of events, find root causes of the problem, and propose possible solutions (including known existing components/libraries, that solve similar problem or can help in solutions).\\n\\nIf there is not enough data to find actual root cause, add debug output and verbose mode if not present, that will allow us to find root cause on next iteration.\\n\\nIf issue related to any other repository/project, where we can report issues on GitHub, please do so. Each issue must contain reproducible examples, workarounds and suggestions for fix the issue in code.\",\"comments\":[],\"title\":\"Our CI/CD triggers on .gitkeep file\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/1528\"}\n{\"body\":\"We do too much CI/CD executed on changes not related to code or docs and so on:\\n\\nThese commits are used in all Pull Requests, as they required to create fork, but CI/CD should not react to them at all. To not waste CI/CD resources.\\n\\n- https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/commit/bd508f23b7599ee0ca22e41e34372071ff5a07c1\\n- https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/commit/26d44bdf3470c91cef02fadb8fc11978208cbf46\\n\\nAlso remove left over `.gitkeep` file, we got in the repository. And double check the logic, so no more leftovers will be in the first place, but if `.gitkeep` file was in the repository before Pull Request, we may as well keep current logic on content reverting, but if you see any logic that can lead to forgotten `.gitkeep` if no such file was before Pull Request - that needs to be fixed.\\n\\nWe need to download all logs and data related about the issue to this repository, make sure we compile that data to `./docs/case-studies/issue-{id}` folder, and use it to do deep case study analysis (also make sure to search online for additional facts and data), in which we will reconstruct timeline/sequence of events, find root causes of the problem, and propose possible solutions (including known existing components/libraries, that solve similar problem or can help in solutions).\\n\\nIf there is not enough data to find actual root cause, add debug output and verbose mode if not present, that will allow us to find root cause on next iteration.\\n\\nIf issue related to any other repository/project, where we can report issues on GitHub, please do so. Each issue must contain reproducible examples, workarounds and suggestions for fix the issue in code.\",\"title\":\"Optimize CI/CD and investigate left over of .gitkeep file\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
