[2026-11-27T21:11:06.409Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_168","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"for language in js rust csharp python java cpp; do printf '\\\\n%s\\\\n' \\\"\"'$language\"; repo=link-foundation/$language-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template; gh issue list --repo \"$repo\" --state all --search '\"'\\\"superseded\\\" \\\"read-only\\\"' --limit 12 --json number,title,url,state --jq '.[]|[.number,.state,.title,.url]|@tsv'; done; gh issue view 2215 --repo link-assistant/hive-mind --json title,body,state,url\"","aggregated_output":"\njs\n289\tCLOSED\tCancel superseded read-only checks on main while preserving active writers\thttps://github.com/link-foundation/js-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template/issues/289\n292\tCLOSED\tAddress all 3 open issues in link-foundation/js-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template\thttps://github.com/link-foundation/js-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template/issues/292\n280\tCLOSED\tA macOS job that never gets a hosted runner fails the release gate and is never retried\thttps://github.com/link-foundation/js-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template/issues/280\n230\tCLOSED\tAdd reusable native JavaScript-first gate and single push gate policy\thttps://github.com/link-foundation/js-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template/issues/230\n\nrust\n230\tCLOSED\tCancel superseded read-only checks on main while preserving active writers\thttps://github.com/link-foundation/rust-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template/issues/230\n232\tCLOSED\tAddress all 2 open issues in link-foundation/rust-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template\thttps://github.com/link-foundation/rust-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template/issues/232\n226\tCLOSED\tA macOS job that never gets a hosted runner fails the release gate and is never retried\thttps://github.com/link-foundation/rust-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template/issues/226\n196\tCLOSED\tAdd reusable native JavaScript-first gate and single push gate policy\thttps://github.com/link-foundation/rust-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template/issues/196\n\ncsharp\n114\tCLOSED\tRunner acquisition classification misses annotations beyond the first API page\thttps://github.com/link-foundation/csharp-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template/issues/114\n79\tCLOSED\tMain concurrency drops pending release runs; pin workflow actions\thttps://github.com/link-foundation/csharp-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template/issues/79\n\npython\n140\tCLOSED\tCancel superseded read-only checks on main while preserving active writers\thttps://github.com/link-foundation/python-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template/issues/140\n142\tCLOSED\tAddress all 2 open issues in link-foundation/python-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template\thttps://github.com/link-foundation/python-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template/issues/142\n42\tCLOSED\tHarden workflow_dispatch inputs and separate check/write concurrency\thttps://github.com/link-foundation/python-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template/issues/42\n\njava\n\ncpp\n41\tCLOSED\tRunner acquisition classification misses annotations beyond the first API page\thttps://github.com/link-foundation/cpp-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template/issues/41\n19\tCLOSED\tA macOS job that never gets a hosted runner fails the release gate and is never retried\thttps://github.com/link-foundation/cpp-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template/issues/19\n{\"body\":\"Fixes #2211\\n\\n## What was wrong\\n\\n`konard/audio-decomposer#1` (\\\"Make a prototype\\\") was solved twice by hive-mind. Both runs opened a pull request, both were auto-merged, and **the complete diff of both was hive-mind's own `.gitkeep` placeholder** — the file the solver writes only so that an empty branch has something to open a pull request from. Nothing was implemented, the issue is still open, and the placeholder is now part of `main`.\\n\\nTwo independent defects had to line up, and both are fixed here.\\n\\n### Bug 1 — the placeholder was reverted *after* the merge\\n\\nOn [audio-decomposer#3](https://github.com/konard/audio-decomposer/pull/3) the branch reads:\\n\\n```\\n19:20:07  798387a0  Initial commit with task details          (.gitkeep touched)\\n19:28:09  2bf2374e  Merge pull request #3                     (.gitkeep on main)\\n19:28:13  79fb66bf  Revert \\\"Initial commit with task details\\\"  <- 4 seconds too late\\n```\\n\\n`src/solve.mjs` called `cleanupClaudeFile()` *after* `startAutoRestartUntilMergeable()`. With `--auto-merge` the loop can only finish by merging, so the revert was structurally guaranteed to lose — this is not a race that sometimes goes the other way. The ordering came from commit `50e3e433` (issue #1516), whose actual requirement is \\\"after `verifyResults()`\\\"; \\\"after the merge loop\\\" was never part of it.\\n\\nThe leak is systematic. `.gitkeep` on the default branch of `link-foundation/rust-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template` — the template `audio-decomposer` was generated from — had accumulated **eight** solver-generated lines from eight merged pull requests between 2026-08-20 and 2026-09-05, one of which (PR #152) also carried real changes.\\n\\n### Bug 2 — an appended placeholder was not recognised as one\\n\\nThe empty-pull-request detector from #2119 matched a placeholder by a single *added* line:\\n\\n```js\\n['.gitkeep', [/^\\\\+#\\\\s*\\\\.gitkeep file auto-generated at .+ for PR creation at branch /m]],\\n```\\n\\n`src/solve.auto-pr.lib.mjs` only writes that line when the file does not exist. When it does — which bug 1 guarantees — it appends `# Updated: <timestamp>` instead, so the auto-generated line is *context*, no pattern matched, and the section counted as real work:\\n\\n```diff\\n@@ -1,3 +1,4 @@\\n # .gitkeep file auto-generated at 2026-08-20T05:02:39.661Z for PR creation at branch issue-136-1491df405bd1 for issue .../issues/136\\n # Updated: 2026-08-22T18:48:37.899Z\\n-# Updated: 2026-08-30T18:52:16.784Z\\n+# Updated: 2026-08-30T18:52:16.784Z\\n+# Updated: 2026-08-30T19:20:07.327Z\\n```\\n\\nThat is the entire diff of the merged PR #3. `hasChanges` was `true`, so the pull request looked mergeable and the auto-restart/resume sequence #2119 built for exactly this situation never fired. The two bugs feed each other: a surviving placeholder forces the append path, which is the blind spot.\\n\\nCodex's refusal to implement anything is out of scope here, per the issue — tracked in #2190.\\n\\n## How to reproduce\\n\\n```bash\\nnode experiments/issue-2211/reproduce-placeholder-not-detected.mjs\\n```\\n\\nIt replays the archived real diffs of audio-decomposer PR #2 and #3 through `measureDiff()`:\\n\\n| Diff  | Before                                                  | After                                                   |\\n| ----- | ------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------- |\\n| PR #2 | `filesChanged: 1, +2, -1` → `hasChanges: true` (merged)  | `filesChanged: 0` → `hasChanges: false, placeholderOnly` |\\n| PR #3 | `filesChanged: 1, +2, -1` → `hasChanges: true` (merged)  | `filesChanged: 0` → `hasChanges: false, placeholderOnly` |\\n\\n`filesChanged: 1` is exactly what GitHub reported for those pull requests, so the pre-fix measurement was faithful and the *classification* was wrong.\\n\\n## The fix\\n\\n- **`src/solve.mjs`** — `cleanupClaudeFile()` moves to immediately before `startAutoRestartUntilMergeable()`, still after `verifyResults()`. Reverting first also lets the loop see the pull request as it really is: with the placeholder gone, a pull request that implemented nothing has an empty diff and the loop restarts the AI.\\n- **`src/solve.auto-merge-guards.lib.mjs`** — new `revertPlaceholderBeforeMerge()`. If the watch loop ever sees `placeholderSections > 0` in its own measurement (a crashed session, an `--auto-continue` resume, a restart inside the loop) it reverts once and re-measures instead of merging.\\n- **`src/pull-request-changes.lib.mjs`** — `measureDiff()` no longer pattern-matches added lines. For a section touching a known placeholder path it reconstructs both sides from the hunks, strips the lines hive-mind generates, and calls it a placeholder only when what remains is identical *and* at least one generated line was involved. Created, appended, re-appended and appended-to-a-repository-owned files are all caught; a genuine edit to either file still counts as work. The stats gained `placeholderSections` so a caller can tell a leftover placeholder from a clean diff. The measurement stays single-pass and copy-free (#2135).\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\n- **`tests/test-placeholder-not-merged-2211.mjs`** (new) — replays the two archived real diffs, then covers every shape the placeholder writer can produce: created `.gitkeep`, appended once, appended to a repository-owned `.gitkeep`, a real edit to `.gitkeep`, created `CLAUDE.md`, a task block appended to a project's `CLAUDE.md`, a real edit to `CLAUDE.md`, and a placeholder sitting next to real work. It also pins both orderings in `src/solve.mjs` and the in-loop guard.\\n- **`tests/test-premature-finish-signaling-1516.mjs`** — asserted the *old* ordering (`cleanup AFTER startAutoRestartUntilMergeable`); it now asserts the invariant that actually belongs to #1516 (after `verifyResults`, before `endWorkSession`) plus the new one from #2211.\\n- **`tests/test-empty-pull-request-2119.mjs`** — unchanged and still passing, so the #2119 behaviour is preserved.\\n\\n## Case study\\n\\n`docs/case-studies/issue-2211/` — the full reconstruction the issue asked for: minute-by-minute timeline, the requirement table with where each is addressed, both root causes traced to the commits that introduced them, the survey of existing components (`git commit --allow-empty` as the structural alternative, unified-diff parsers and why they were not adopted, the prior hive-mind work in #1436/#1791/#1516/#2119/#2135), and the notes on the two polluted upstream repositories. All raw evidence is archived verbatim under `docs/case-studies/issue-2211/data/`.\\n\",\"state\":\"MERGED\",\"title\":\"fix(2211): never merge the solver placeholder, and restart when nothing changed\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/pull/2215\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
