[2026-11-27T21:11:17.708Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_175","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat .github/scripts/pipeline-status.mjs; sed -n '388,413p' dev/log/issues/207/pulls/208/templates/CI-CD-BEST-PRACTICES.md; sed -n '1,105p' .github/workflows/javascript-stage.yml; ls -a | head -40; git status --porcelain=v1 --untracked-files=normal\"","aggregated_output":"import { resolve } from 'node:path';\nimport { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url';\n\n/** A failed prerequisite must never turn the remaining skipped jobs green. */\nexport function checkPipeline(needs) {\n  if (!needs || typeof needs !== 'object' || Array.isArray(needs) || !Object.keys(needs).length) {\n    throw Error('Missing pipeline job results');\n  }\n  const failed = Object.entries(needs).filter(\n    ([, job]) => !['success', 'skipped'].includes(job?.result),\n  );\n  if (failed.length)\n    throw Error(\n      `Pipeline jobs did not succeed: ${failed.map(([name, job]) => `${name} (${job?.result ?? 'missing'})`).join(', ')}`,\n    );\n  if (!Object.values(needs).some((job) => job.result === 'success'))\n    throw Error('Every pipeline job was skipped; no verification ran');\n  return Object.entries(needs)\n    .filter(([, job]) => job.result === 'skipped')\n    .map(([name]) => name);\n}\n\nif (process.argv[1] && resolve(process.argv[1]) === fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)) {\n  try {\n    const skipped = checkPipeline(JSON.parse(process.env.NEEDS_JSON || '{}'));\n    if (skipped.length)\n      console.log(\n        `::notice::Conditional jobs skipped: ${skipped.join(', ')}. See their event, path and prerequisite conditions above.`,\n      );\n    console.log('All executed pipeline jobs succeeded.');\n  } catch (error) {\n    console.error(error.message);\n    process.exitCode = 1;\n  }\n}\n  await run('git', ['pull', '--rebase', remote, branch]);\n}\n```\n\n- **Never `--force`, and never `--force-with-lease`, on a shared branch.** Both turn a lost race into a silent deletion of whatever the writer ahead of you landed. Rebasing is the point: the later commit has to end up on top of the earlier one.\n- **Recompute after the rebase whatever was derived before it.** A version number, a changelog entry or a tag chosen against the stale tip may already be taken by the writer that won the queue. Re-read the state instead of replaying the plan.\n- **Report success only after the push landed.** A step that sets `version_committed=true` before the push is confirmed leaves the downstream publish job working from a commit that exists only on that runner.\n- **Bound the retries and name the reason in the log.** A handful of attempts with a short delay covers a queue; an unbounded loop against a branch that is genuinely protected turns a fast failure into a long one.\n\n#### Preserve a full check when a commit arrives\n\nGroup commit checks by workflow and PR and cancel only superseded `synchronize` runs. Give ready and manual runs a per-run key so GitHub also preserves queued runs. Group pushes by SHA so each main revision keeps its checks.\n\n```yaml\nconcurrency:\n  group: ci-${{ github.workflow }}-${{ github.event.pull_request.number || github.ref }}-${{ github.event_name }}-${{ github.event.action || 'run' }}-${{ (github.event_name == 'pull_request' && github.event.action == 'synchronize' && 'latest') || (github.event_name == 'push' && github.sha) || github.run_id }}\n  cancel-in-progress: ${{ github.event_name == 'pull_request' && github.event.action == 'synchronize' }}\n```\n\nApply this grouping to each cancellable job if the workflow uses job-level groups, keeping the job and any matrix identity in its key. Keep the shared non-cancelling group for publishing and deployment jobs. Workflow-level cancellation is safe only when every event eligible for cancellation runs checks without publishing or deploying. See the [language template patches](../examples/ci-cd-pull-request-tiers/README.md).\n\n### 11. Secrets Detection\n\nPrevent accidental credential leaks in CI:\n\n- Include a secrets scan step using tools like `secretlint` or `truffleHog`\nname: JavaScript stage\n\n# The JavaScript stage of the stage gate (issue #111): ESLint and Prettier,\n# every Node unit test (`npm run test:js`) and the cross-language parity\n# checker. It needs no Rust, wasm-pack or .NET, so it finishes in a few\n# minutes.\n#\n# Every workflow that runs Rust or C# calls this file as its first job\n# (`javascript: uses: ./.github/workflows/javascript-stage.yml`) and lists\n# `javascript` in the `needs:` of each Rust or C# job, so those jobs start\n# only after this stage succeeded for the same commit. A failed, cancelled or\n# skipped stage leaves them skipped. .github/scripts/workflow-policy.test.mjs\n# enforces that wiring. javascript.yml runs the same stage on its own for\n# every pull request, with no path filter, behind the required\n# \"Pipeline Status (javascript)\" check.\n\non:\n  workflow_call:\n\npermissions:\n  contents: read\n\n# Provide Git config to actions/checkout itself; checkout runs git init before\n# any workflow step can configure Git, which otherwise prints the\n# default-branch hint into every log.\nenv:\n  GIT_CONFIG_COUNT: '1'\n  GIT_CONFIG_KEY_0: ini…nch\n  GIT_CONFIG_VALUE_0: main\n\njobs:\n  stage:\n    name: JavaScript stage\n    runs-on: ubuntu-24.04\n    timeout-minutes: 15\n    # In a called workflow, github.workflow is the caller's name, so each\n    # caller cancels only its own superseded stage.\n    concurrency:\n      group: check-${{ github.workflow }}-${{ github.event_name == 'pull_request' && github.event.action == 'synchronize' && github.ref || github.event_name == 'push' && github.sha || github.run_id }}-javascript-stage\n      cancel-in-progress: ${{ github.event_name == 'pull_request' && github.event.action == 'synchronize' }}\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v7\n        with:\n          persist-credentials: false\n          # The parity checker compares the manifest with the base commit.\n          fetch-depth: 0\n\n      - name: Setup Node.js\n        uses: actions/setup-node@v7\n        with:\n          node-version: '26.x'\n          cache: npm\n          cache-dependency-path: js/package-lock.json\n\n      - name: Install npm dependencies\n        working-directory: js\n        run: npm ci\n\n      - name: Lint and format check\n        working-directory: js\n        run: npm run lint\n\n      # js/test, csharp/scripts, .github/scripts and parity unit tests. Until\n      # issue #111 these ran only inside wasm.yml, after a Rust toolchain and\n      # wasm-pack install.\n      # js/test/golden-fixtures.test.mjs writes the receipt of the fixtures\n      # it loaded; the next step proves none was skipped (docs/PARITY.md).\n      - name: Test JavaScript\n        working-directory: js\n        env:\n          GOLDEN_FIXTURES_RECEIPT: ${{ runner.temp }}/golden-javascript.json\n        run: npm run test:js\n\n      - name: Check that the JavaScript suite loaded every golden fixture\n        env:\n          RECEIPT: ${{ runner.temp }}/golden-javascript.json\n        run: node parity/check-parity.mjs --receipt javascript \"$RECEIPT\"\n\n      # Fails on a one-sided feature change, a stale fingerprint, an\n      # unassigned source file or a drifted golden fixture (docs/PARITY.md).\n      # Pull requests compare with their base; pushes with the previous tip.\n      - name: Check cross-language parity\n        env:\n          PARITY_BASE_SHA: ${{ github.event.pull_request.base.sha || github.event.before }}\n          PARITY_DEBUG: ${{ runner.debug }}\n        run: node parity/check-parity.mjs\n.\n..\n.git\n.gitattributes\n.github\n.gitignore\n.lycheeignore\n.package-registry-manager.json\n.pre-commit-config.yaml\n.secretlintrc.json\nAGENTS.md\nCLAUDE.md\nCONTRIBUTING.md\nLICENSE\nREADME.md\ncsharp\ndev\ndocs\nexamples\nexperiments\njs\nparity\nrust\n M .github/scripts/ci-governance.test.mjs\n M .github/scripts/npm-release.test.mjs\n M .github/scripts/verify-npm-trust.mjs\n M .github/scripts/verify-npm-trust.test.mjs\n M .github/scripts/workflow-policy.test.mjs\n M .github/workflows/crash.yml\n M .github/workflows/csharp.yml\n M .github/workflows/deep-client.yml\n M .github/workflows/dependencies.yml\n M .github/workflows/docs.yml\n M .github/workflows/ipc.yml\n M .github/workflows/javascript-stage.yml\n M .github/workflows/javascript.yml\n M .github/workflows/js-client.yml\n M .github/workflows/js-server.yml\n M .github/workflows/links.yml\n M .github/workflows/rerun-infrastructure-failures.yml\n M .github/workflows/rust.yml\n M .github/workflows/security.yml\n M .github/workflows/wasm.yml\n M .github/workflows/workflows.yml\nD  .gitkeep\n M csharp/Foundation.Data.Doublets.Cli/CliIo.cs\n M csharp/Foundation.Data.Doublets.Cli/Program.cs\n M experiments/issue-138/etcd-cluster.mjs\n M experiments/issue-138/etcd-harness.mjs\n M experiments/issue-138/etcd-harness.test.mjs\n M parity/features.json\n M rust/src/transactions/mod.rs\n?? csharp/.changeset/ci-reliability.md\n?? dev/log/issues/207/\n?? rust/changelog.d/20261127_210000_ci_reliability.md\n?? rust/src/transactions/tests.rs\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
