[2026-11-27T21:12:29.003Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_187","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"mkdir -p /tmp/link-cli-207-reports\ncat > /tmp/link-cli-207-reports/concurrency.md <<'EOF'\nThe current workflow uses a branch-ref concurrency key and \"'`cancel-in-progress: true` for read-only checks running on `main`. Two commits share the same key, so the later commit can cancel checks for the earlier commit. A release commit can cause this even when no other contributor is pushing. The release writer'\"'s own queue cannot recover a prerequisite that was cancelled.\n\nThe issue was observed in an adopter, link-foundation/link-cli#207. Its [JS conformance run](https://github.com/link-foundation/link-cli/actions/runs/46059980457) and [Rust pipeline](https://github.com/link-foundation/link-cli/actions/runs/46059980682) lost checks around overlapping default-branch updates. The template job linked above has the same concurrency policy.\n\n### Reproduce in a disposable repository\n\nCopy the cited workflow into a fork or test repository. Add \"'`run: sleep 30` as the first step of its read-only check if it completes quickly. With publication disabled in the disposable repository, push two distinct qualifying commits to its default branch while the first check is running. Follow both runs with `gh run list --branch main --limit 5` and inspect the check results. On workflows with push path filters, update the workflow in both commits so both trigger it. Repeat with a manual run and a push or with two manual runs to check whether the branch key also conflates those events.\n\n### Workaround and proposed change\n\nSpace pushes until the earlier run finishes as a temporary workaround. Use the key below in the template for each read-only job, retaining its matrix suffix where relevant. Keep writers on their existing shared repository queue.\n\n```yaml\nconcurrency:\n  group: check-${{ github.workflow }}-${{ (github.event_name == '\"'pull_request' && github.event.action == 'synchronize' && github.ref) || (github.event_name == 'push' && github.sha) || github.run_id }}-check\n  cancel-in-progress: \"'${{ github.event_name == '\"'pull_request' && github.event.action == 'synchronize' }}\n\"'```\n\nA policy test can require per-SHA main checks, independent manual and ready runs, PR synchronization replacement, and retention of matrix and job suffixes. See the guide'\"'s [preserve a full check when a commit arrives](https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/blob/main/docs/CI-CD-BEST-PRACTICES.md#preserve-a-full-check-when-a-commit-arrives) and [GitHub's concurrency semantics](https://docs.github.com/en/actions/how-tos/write-workflows/choose-when-workflows-run/control-workflow-concurrency).\nEOF\nfor lang in rust js csharp python java cpp; do\n  repo=\\\"link-foundation/\"'$lang-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template\"\n  case \"$lang\" in\n    rust) spec=release.yml:549; prior=230;;\n    js) spec=release.yml:305; prior=289;;\n    csharp) spec=release.yml:186; prior=79;;\n    python) spec=release.yml:299; prior=140;;\n    java) spec=release.yml:146; prior=5;;\n    cpp) spec=workflows.yml:43; prior=13;;\n  esac\n  sha=$(jq -r .sha \"dev/log/issues/207/pulls/208/templates/$lang-tree.json\")\n  workflow=${spec%:*}\n  line=${spec#*:}\n  printf '\"'Pinned template evidence is in [\"'`%s`, line %s](https://github.com/%s/blob/%s/.github/workflows/%s#L%s). This concerns the current checks policy after #%s.'\"\\\\n\\\\n' \\\"\"'$workflow\" \"$line\" \"$repo\" \"$sha\" \"$workflow\" \"$line\" \"$prior\" > \"/tmp/link-cli-207-reports/$lang.md\"\n  cat /tmp/link-cli-207-reports/concurrency.md >> \"/tmp/link-cli-207-reports/$lang.md\"\n  printf '\"'%s\\\\t' \\\"\"'$lang\"\n  gh issue create --repo \"$repo\" --title '\"'Keep default-branch checks for each commit and preserve manual runs' --body-file \\\"/tmp/link-cli-207-reports/\"'$lang.md\"\ndone > /tmp/link-cli-207-upstream-issues.tsv 2>/tmp/link-cli-207-upstream-issues.err\n'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
