l_request' && github.event.action == 'synchronize' && github.ref) || (github.event_name == 'push' && github.sha) || github.run_id }}-check\n  cancel-in-progress: \"'${{ github.event_name == '\"'pull_request' && github.event.action == 'synchronize' }}\n\"'```\n\nA policy test can require per-SHA main checks, independent manual and ready runs, PR synchronization replacement, and retention of matrix and job suffixes. See the guide'\"'s [preserve a full check when a commit arrives](https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/blob/main/docs/CI-CD-BEST-PRACTICES.md#preserve-a-full-check-when-a-commit-arrives) and [GitHub's concurrency semantics](https://docs.github.com/en/actions/how-tos/write-workflows/choose-when-workflows-run/control-workflow-concurrency).\nEOF\nfor lang in rust js csharp python java cpp; do\n  repo=\\\"link-foundation/\"'$lang-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template\"\n  case \"$lang\" in\n    rust) spec=release.yml:549; prior=230;;\n    js) spec=release.yml:305; prior=289;;\n    csharp) spec=release.yml:186; prior=79;;\n    python) spec=release.yml:299; prior=140;;\n    java) spec=release.yml:146; prior=5;;\n    cpp) spec=workflows.yml:43; prior=13;;\n  esac\n  sha=$(jq -r .sha \"dev/log/issues/207/pulls/208/templates/$lang-tree.json\")\n  workflow=${spec%:*}\n  line=${spec#*:}\n  printf '\"'Pinned template evidence is in [\"'`%s`, line %s](https://github.com/%s/blob/%s/.github/workflows/%s#L%s). This concerns the current checks policy after #%s.'\"\\\\n\\\\n' \\\"\"'$workflow\" \"$line\" \"$repo\" \"$sha\" \"$workflow\" \"$line\" \"$prior\" > \"/tmp/link-cli-207-reports/$lang.md\"\n  cat /tmp/link-cli-207-reports/concurrency.md >> \"/tmp/link-cli-207-reports/$lang.md\"\n  printf '\"'%s\\\\t' \\\"\"'$lang\"\n  gh issue create --repo \"$repo\" --title '\"'Keep default-branch checks for each commit and preserve manual runs' --body-file \\\"/tmp/link-cli-207-reports/\"'$lang.md\"\ndone > /tmp/link-cli-207-upstream-issues.tsv 2>/tmp/link-cli-207-upstream