[2026-11-27T21:18:05.824Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_249","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '41,155p' dev/log/issues/207/pulls/208/templates/CI-CD-BEST-PRACTICES.md\nsed -n '1,80p' .github/workflows/js-client.yml\ntail -n 8 /tmp/link-cli-207-{clippy,secretlint}.log\ngit diff --cached --stat | tail -3\"","aggregated_output":"\n### 1. Run Checks Only on Relevant File Changes\n\n**Only trigger checks when relevant files change.** This dramatically reduces CI costs and run times.\n\nUse a `detect-changes` job at the start of your workflow to determine which file categories changed:\n\n```yaml\njobs:\n  detect-changes:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-24.04\n    outputs:\n      code-changed: ${{ steps.changes.outputs.code }}\n      docs-changed: ${{ steps.changes.outputs.docs }}\n      docker-changed: ${{ steps.changes.outputs.docker }}\n      workflow-changed: ${{ steps.changes.outputs.workflow }}\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v4\n        with:\n          fetch-depth: 2\n      - name: Detect changes\n        id: changes\n        run: node scripts/detect-code-changes.mjs\n```\n\nThen gate each job on the relevant output:\n\n```yaml\ntest-suites:\n  needs: [detect-changes]\n  if: needs.detect-changes.outputs.code-changed == 'true' || needs.detect-changes.outputs.workflow-changed == 'true'\n  # ...\n\nvalidate-docs:\n  needs: [detect-changes]\n  if: needs.detect-changes.outputs.docs-changed == 'true'\n  # ...\n\ndocker-pr-check:\n  needs: [detect-changes]\n  if: needs.detect-changes.outputs.docker-changed == 'true' || needs.detect-changes.outputs.workflow-changed == 'true'\n  # ...\n```\n\n**What to exclude from \"code changes\" detection:**\n\n- Markdown files (`*.md`) — documentation-only changes don't need changeset files\n- `.changeset/` folder — changeset metadata isn't code\n- `data/` and `experiments/` folders — non-production content\n- `.gitkeep` files — placeholder files with no functional impact\n\n**What always triggers checks when changed:**\n\n- Source code files (`.mjs`, `.ts`, `.py`, `.rs`, `.go`, etc.)\n- `package.json` / dependency manifests\n- CI/CD workflow files (`.github/workflows/*.yml`)\n- `Dockerfile` and related infrastructure files\n\n#### Commit and ready-for-review checks\n\n- **Commit tier (`synchronize`)** runs lint, type checking, and fast unit tests for changed packages, including on draft PRs. Aim for a 5–10 minute critical path.\n- **Ready tier (`ready_for_review`)** runs the heavy unit, integration, and end-to-end suites. Open the PR as a draft and mark it ready when the full check should start.\n\nOmit `opened`, `reopened`, and `edited` from these workflows. To run the heavy tier again after a new commit, switch the PR to draft and mark it ready again, or dispatch the checks explicitly. Keep full release validation on `main` and keep a checks-only manual mode separate from publishing.\n\n```yaml\non:\n  pull_request:\n    types: [synchronize, ready_for_review]\n  push:\n    branches: [main]\n  workflow_dispatch:\n```\n\nThe ready run tests the revision that triggered it. If full verification is required to merge, require a full-tier check for the current revision. A green commit-tier run alone cannot satisfy that requirement. A manual run must target the intended PR revision or merge result.\n\n#### Select monorepo suites from the workspace graph\n\nHave a planner read workspace manifests (for example, each package's `package.json`) and map changed paths to their owning packages.\n\n- Schedule a package's unit suite when the package itself changes.\n- For integration tests, walk dependencies in reverse from each changed package. Test the changed packages and every transitive consumer, visiting each package once even if the graph has cycles.\n- Run every suite when a changed path is unclassified or the planner cannot establish the graph or diff. Explicitly classify shared inputs such as the lockfile, workspace config, and common test setup as affecting all packages.\n\nEmit JSON job matrices, with `[]` for an empty selection, and use the planner outputs to gate and shard jobs. For example, `test-db` can contain `[{ \"package\": \"api\", \"shard\": \"1/2\" }, { \"package\": \"api\", \"shard\": \"2/2\" }]`.\n\n```yaml\ntest-db:\n  needs: [plan]\n  if: ${{ !cancelled() && needs.plan.outputs.test-db != '[]' && (github.event_name != 'pull_request' || github.event.action == 'ready_for_review') }}\n  strategy:\n    matrix:\n      include: ${{ fromJSON(needs.plan.outputs.test-db) }}\n  # ...\n```\n\n### 2. File Size Limits\n\n**Enforce a maximum of 1000-1500 lines per code file.**\n\nThis constraint benefits both AI and human developers:\n\n- AI models can read and understand entire files within context windows\n- Humans can navigate and comprehend files without cognitive overload\n- Forces modular, well-organized code architecture\n\nExample enforcement in CI (bash):\n\n```bash\nfind src/ -name \"*.mjs\" -type f | while read -r file; do\n  line_count=$(wc -l < \"$file\")\n  if [ \"$line_count\" -gt 1500 ]; then\n    echo \"ERROR: $file has $line_count lines (limit: 1500)\"\n    echo \"::error file=$file::File has $line_count lines (limit: 1500)\"\n    exit 1\nname: JS client CI\n\n# @link-foundation/link-cli-client (js/client, issue #108): unit tests and\n# type checks, the conformance runner on Node.js, Bun and Deno against the\n# Rust and C# `clink --serve` and the WebAssembly `Clink`, a smoke run of the\n# synthetic consumer, and the npm release of the package.\non:\n  # Only main on push: PR branches are covered by the pull_request trigger\n  # (issue #96).\n  push:\n    branches:\n      - main\n    paths:\n      - '.github/workflows/js-client.yml'\n      - '.github/scripts/**'\n      - '.github/workflows/javascript-stage.yml'\n      - 'parity/**'\n      - 'js/package*.json'\n      - 'js/client/**'\n      - 'examples/composition/**'\n      - 'rust/**'\n      - 'csharp/**'\n      - 'docs/protocol/**'\n      - 'examples/cluster-csharp/**'\n      - 'examples/journal-maintenance-csharp/**'\n      - 'examples/journal-reclamation-csharp/**'\n      - 'examples/sqlite-csharp/**'\n      - 'examples/native-lsm-js/**'\n      - 'examples/journal-chunks/**'\n      - 'examples/native-pages/**'\n      - 'examples/native-pages-csharp/**'\n      - 'examples/sorted-tables/**'\n      - 'examples/sorted-tables-csharp/**'\n      - 'examples/journal-checkpoints/**'\n      - 'experiments/issue-138/**'\n  pull_request:\n    branches:\n      - main\n    paths:\n      - '.github/workflows/js-client.yml'\n      - '.github/scripts/**'\n      - '.github/workflows/javascript-stage.yml'\n      - 'parity/**'\n      - 'js/package*.json'\n      - 'js/client/**'\n      - 'examples/composition/**'\n      - 'rust/**'\n      - 'csharp/**'\n      - 'docs/protocol/**'\n      - 'examples/cluster-csharp/**'\n      - 'examples/journal-maintenance-csharp/**'\n      - 'examples/journal-reclamation-csharp/**'\n      - 'examples/sqlite-csharp/**'\n      - 'examples/native-lsm-js/**'\n      - 'examples/journal-chunks/**'\n      - 'examples/native-pages/**'\n      - 'examples/native-pages-csharp/**'\n      - 'examples/sorted-tables/**'\n      - 'examples/sorted-tables-csharp/**'\n      - 'examples/journal-checkpoints/**'\n      - 'experiments/issue-138/**'\n  workflow_dispatch:\n    inputs:\n      verbose_consensus:\n        description: 'Record etcd election status and member debug logs'\n        type: boolean\n        default: false\n      verify_trusted_publishing:\n        description: 'Verify npm OIDC authentication without publishing'\n        type: boolean\n        default: false\n\n# Read-only concurrency cancels superseded PR synchronizations. Each main\n# revision keeps its results. Release writers share the repository queue.\n\n# Least privilege by default; the release job opts into more below.\npermissions:\n  contents: read\n\n# Provide Git config to actions/checkout itself; checkout runs git init before\n==> /tmp/link-cli-207-clippy.log <==\n    Checking adler2 v2.0.1\n    Checking fastrand v2.5.0\n    Checking tempfile v3.27.0\n    Checking miniz_oxide v0.9.1\n    Checking http v1.5.0\n   Compiling clap_derive v4.6.9\n    Checking clap_builder v4.6.10\n    Checking rustls-webpki v0.103.17\n\n==> /tmp/link-cli-207-secretlint.log <==\n rust/src/transactions/mod.rs                       |  55 +-\n rust/src/transactions/tests.rs                     |  52 ++\n 162 files changed, 2062 insertions(+), 415 deletions(-)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
