.github/scripts` to exercise the policy.\n- Run `npm --prefix js run lint`, `npm --prefix js run test:js`, `node parity/check-parity.mjs --base origin/main`, and `npm pack --dry-run` from each npm package directory.\n- This environment has no installed pre-commit hooks. The relevant checks were run manually, including workflow policy, JavaScript and Python quality, secrets, Rust formatting and lint, .NET formatting on the CI SDK, Actionlint and zizmor.\n\n## Registry setup still needed\n\nThe npm server package is absent from the public registry, and its OIDC exchange returns HTTP 404. An npm scope maintainer needs to publish the first public version, configure GitHub trusted publishing for `link-foundation/link-cli` and `js-server.yml`, and run JS server CI on `main` with **Verify npm trusted publishing** enabled before retrying the main workflow. The PR’s tarball and code checks run independently. The real publishing criterion remains open until the maintainer steps and main verification succeed. [Failed preflight](https://github.com/link-foundation/link-cli/actions/runs/46067149214)\n\n## Evidence and upstream reports\n\n- [Investigation, timeline and requirements](https://github.com/link-foundation/link-cli/blob/issue-207-ac4b1e2ba1ef/docs/case-studies/issue-207/README.md)\n- [Run logs, template file comparison and local verification](https://github.com/link-foundation/link-cli/blob/issue-207-ac4b1e2ba1ef/dev/log/issues/207/pulls/208/README.md)\n- [Rust template #275](https://github.com/link-foundation/rust-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template/issues/275), [JS template #325](https://github.com/link-foundation/js-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template/issues/325), [C# template #121](https://github.com/link-foundation/csharp-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template/issues/121), [Python template #173](https://github.com/link-foundation/python-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template/issues/173), [Java template #39](https://github.com/link-foundation/java-ai-drive