[2026-11-27T21:34:42.784Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_495","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,145p' .github/workflows/rerun-infrastructure-failures.yml && jq -r '.jobs[]|[.name,.status,.conclusion]|@tsv' dev/log/issues/207/pulls/208/ci-logs/runs/46067862699.json && zcat dev/log/issues/207/pulls/208/ci-logs/runs/46067862699.log.gz | sed -n '133,167p'\"","aggregated_output":"name: Rerun infrastructure failures\n\n# Ported from the Rust pipeline template (#226), for link-cli issue #165.\n# When GitHub has no hosted runner to give (macOS arm64 capacity is\n# the usual case) it gives up on a queued job with \"The job was not acquired by\n# Runner of type hosted even after multiple attempts\". The job ends cancelled\n# with no steps and no runner, so no code ran, yet the release and status gates\n# go red and nothing reruns them. This workflow reruns such a run's failed jobs\n# (and, through `gh run rerun --failed`, the gates that depend on them) at most\n# twice. A job that ran steps and failed never triggers a rerun; see\n# .github/scripts/unacquired-jobs.py for the exact rule.\n#\n# workflow_run is safe here: the checkout is the default branch (github.sha of a\n# workflow_run event), nothing from the triggering run is executed, and the job\n# only reads that run through the API and asks GitHub to rerun it.\non: # zizmor: ignore[dangerous-triggers]\n  workflow_run:\n    # Every workflow with a terminal Pipeline Status gate.\n    workflows:\n      - JavaScript\n      - Rust CI/CD Pipeline\n      - C# CI/CD Pipeline\n      - JS client CI\n      - JS server CI\n      - DeepClient CI\n      - WebAssembly CI\n      - Docs\n      - Dependencies\n      - Workflows\n      - Security\n      - Broken Link Checker\n      - Crash tests\n      - IPC\n    types: [completed]\n\npermissions:\n  contents: read\n\n# Configure checkout's git init before the first step runs.\nenv:\n  GIT_CONFIG_COUNT: '1'\n  GIT_CONFIG_KEY_0: ini…nch\n  GIT_CONFIG_VALUE_0: main\n\njobs:\n  rerun:\n    name: Rerun jobs that never got a runner\n    # The status gate turns the run into a failure when a job was not acquired.\n    # The script reruns attempts 1 and 2 and reports an error on attempt 3.\n    if: github.event.workflow_run.conclusion == 'failure'\n    runs-on: ubuntu-24.04\n    timeout-minutes: 5\n    concurrency:\n      group: rerun-infrastructure-failures-${{ github.event.workflow_run.id }}\n      cancel-in-progress: false\n    permissions:\n      contents: read\n      # Read the run's jobs and rerun them.\n      actions: write\n      # Read each job's check-run annotations.\n      checks: read\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v7\n        with:\n          ref: ${{ github.sha }}\n          persist-credentials: false\n\n      - name: Rerun jobs that GitHub never handed to a runner\n        env:\n          GH_TOKEN: ${{ github.token }}\n          REPOSITORY: ${{ github.repository }}\n          RUN_ID: ${{ github.event.workflow_run.id }}\n          ATTEMPT: ${{ github.event.workflow_run.run_attempt }}\n          UNACQUIRED_JOBS_VERBOSE: ${{ vars.UNACQUIRED_JOBS_VERBOSE || '0' }}\n        run: >-\n          python3 .github/scripts/unacquired-jobs.py rerun\n          --repository \"$REPOSITORY\" --run-id \"$RUN_ID\" --attempt \"$ATTEMPT\"\n\n\n  pipeline-status:\n    name: Pipeline Status (rerun-infrastructure-failures)\n    needs:\n      - rerun\n    if: ${{ !cancelled() && github.event.workflow_run.conclusion == 'failure' }}\n    runs-on: ubuntu-24.04\n    timeout-minutes: 5\n    concurrency:\n      group: check-${{ github.workflow }}-${{ github.event_name == 'pull_request' && github.event.action == 'synchronize' && github.ref || github.event_name == 'push' && github.sha || github.run_id }}-pipeline-status\n      cancel-in-progress: ${{ github.event_name == 'pull_request' && github.event.action == 'synchronize' }}\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v7\n        with:\n          persist-credentials: false\n      - uses: actions/setup-node@v7\n        with:\n          node-version: '26.x'\n      - name: Check every prerequisite\n        working-directory: .\n        env:\n          NEEDS_JSON: ${{ toJSON(needs) }}\n        run: node .github/scripts/pipeline-status.mjs\nRerun jobs that never got a runner\tcompleted\tsuccess\nPipeline Status (rerun-infrastructure-failures)\tcompleted\tsuccess\nRerun jobs that never got a runner\tRun actions/checkout@v7\t2026-11-27T21:04:36.3126174Z [command]/usr/bin/git submodule foreach --recursive sh -c \"git config --local --name-only --get-regexp 'http\\.https\\:\\/\\/github\\.com\\/\\.extraheader' && git config --local --unset-all 'http.https://github.com/.extraheader' || :\"\nRerun jobs that never got a runner\tRun actions/checkout@v7\t2026-11-27T21:04:36.3340084Z Removing includeIf entries pointing to credentials config files\nRerun jobs that never got a runner\tRun actions/checkout@v7\t2026-11-27T21:04:36.3343725Z [command]/usr/bin/git config --local --name-only --get-regexp ^includeIf\\.gitdir:\nRerun jobs that never got a runner\tRun actions/checkout@v7\t2026-11-27T21:04:36.3377864Z includeif.gitdir:/home/runner/work/link-cli/link-cli/.git.path\nRerun jobs that never got a runner\tRun actions/checkout@v7\t2026-11-27T21:04:36.3378523Z includeif.gitdir:/home/runner/work/link-cli/link-cli/.git/worktrees/*.path\nRerun jobs that never got a runner\tRun actions/checkout@v7\t2026-11-27T21:04:36.3378881Z includeif.gitdir:/github/workspace/.git.path\nRerun jobs that never got a runner\tRun actions/checkout@v7\t2026-11-27T21:04:36.3379311Z includeif.gitdir:/github/workspace/.git/worktrees/*.path\nRerun jobs that never got a runner\tRun actions/checkout@v7\t2026-11-27T21:04:36.3389059Z [command]/usr/bin/git config --local --get-all includeif.gitdir:/home/runner/work/link-cli/link-cli/.git.path\nRerun jobs that never got a runner\tRun actions/checkout@v7\t2026-11-27T21:04:36.3421980Z /home/runner/work/_temp/git-credential