[2026-11-27T21:41:22.833Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_553","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,140p' experiments/issue-207/compare-ci-files.py && sed -n '1,6p' dev/log/issues/207/pulls/208/templates/ci-file-comparison.tsv && git diff --unified=3 HEAD -- docs/case-studies/issue-207/README.md dev/log/issues/207/pulls/208/README.md\"","aggregated_output":"\"\"\"Inventory CI inputs from link-cli and downloaded recursive template trees.\"\"\"\n\nimport json\nimport re\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2]\nTEMPLATES = (\"rust\", \"js\", \"csharp\", \"python\", \"java\", \"cpp\")\n\n\ndef ci_input(path: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Include workflow-owned files, CI helpers, hooks, and root CI policies.\"\"\"\n    return (\n        path.startswith((\".github/\", \"scripts/\", \"parity/\"))\n        or re.match(r\"^(csharp|js|rust)/scripts/\", path) is not None\n        or re.search(\n            r\"^\\.(pre-commit|lychee|secretlint|actionlint|zizmor|codecov|package-registry-manager)\",\n            path,\n        )\n        is not None\n    )\n\n\ndef stem(path: str) -> str:\n    return Path(path).stem.replace(\"_\", \"-\")\n\n\ndef purpose(path: str) -> str:\n    matched = (\n        (\n            \"change detection and stage gate\",\n            r\"detect|fresh-merge|javascript-first|javascript-stage|parity\",\n        ),\n        (\n            \"registry and release\",\n            r\"version|changelog|changeset|release|publish|registry|npm|pypi|nuget|crates|vcpkg|maven|package\",\n        ),\n        (\n            \"workflow validation and status\",\n            r\"workflow|status|gate|policy|concurrency|zizmor|actionlint\",\n        ),\n        (\n            \"security and dependencies\",\n            r\"security|secrets|codeql|audit|depend|sarif|credential|preflight\",\n        ),\n        (\"documentation and links\", r\"docs|lychee|links|web-archive|pages\"),\n        (\n            \"runner and artifact handling\",\n            r\"runner|unacquired|rerun|artifact|archive|budget|buildx\",\n        ),\n        (\n            \"source and test quality\",\n            r\"lint|format|file-size|line-limit|coverage|warnings|test\",\n        ),\n    )\n    for description, pattern in matched:\n        if re.search(pattern, path):\n            return description\n    return \"repository or language-specific infrastructure\"\n\n\ndef main() -> None:\n    directory = Path(sys.argv[1])\n    base = sys.argv[2]\n    local_tree = subprocess.check_output(\n        [\"git\", \"ls-tree\", \"-rz\", base], cwd=ROOT, text=True\n    )\n    local = {}\n    for entry in local_tree.rstrip(\"\\0\").split(\"\\0\"):\n        metadata, path = entry.split(\"\\t\", 1)\n        if ci_input(path):\n            local[path] = metadata.split()[2]\n    snapshots = {\"link-cli\": local}\n    template_paths = {}\n    for name in TEMPLATES:\n        tree = json.loads((directory / f\"{name}-tree.json\").read_text())[\"tree\"]\n        snapshot = {\n            file[\"path\"]: file[\"sha\"]\n            for file in tree\n            if file[\"type\"] == \"blob\" and ci_input(file[\"path\"])\n        }\n        template_paths.update(\n            {f\"{name}/{path}\": digest for path, digest in snapshot.items()}\n        )\n        snapshots[name] = snapshot\n\n    print(\"repository\\tpath\\tblob\\tpurpose\\tother repository matches\")\n    for name, snapshot in snapshots.items():\n        other = template_paths if name == \"link-cli\" else local\n        for path, blob in sorted(snapshot.items()):\n            peers = [\n                f\"{item} ({'identical' if digest == blob else 'same stem'})\"\n                for item, digest in other.items()\n                if digest == blob or stem(item) == stem(path)\n            ]\n            print(name, path, blob, purpose(path), \", \".join(peers) or \"-\", sep=\"\\t\")\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\nrepository\tpath\tblob\tpurpose\tother repository matches\nlink-cli\t.github/CODEOWNERS\t410a3e124e2f6fc3551acc696d681328602ea0ee\trepository or language-specific infrastructure\t-\nlink-cli\t.github/codecov.yml\t927b361e25322e61525d875dee272d0b5a0caf58\trepository or language-specific infrastructure\t-\nlink-cli\t.github/codeql/codeql-config.yml\t2b1f4c19a2399eae33632dfffa725258523e50ad\tsecurity and dependencies\trust/.github/codeql/codeql-config.yml (same stem), js/.github/codeql/codeql-config.yml (same stem), python/.github/codeql/codeql-config.yml (same stem)\nlink-cli\t.github/dependabot.yml\t45f3a5cc8b687627104b23865705b7036e60068a\tsecurity and dependencies\trust/.github/dependabot.yml (same stem), csharp/.github/dependabot.yml (same stem), python/.github/dependabot.yml (same stem), java/.github/dependabot.yml (same stem), cpp/.github/dependabot.yml (same stem)\nlink-cli\t.github/scripts/audit-nuget-dependencies.mjs\t41c6c2f069a130e266aed45d8541086abad9310c\tregistry and release\t-\ndiff --git a/dev/log/issues/207/pulls/208/README.md b/dev/log/issues/207/pulls/208/README.md\nindex b94df510..db28aa7a 100644\n--- a/dev/log/issues/207/pulls/208/README.md\n+++ b/dev/log/issues/207/pulls/208/README.md\n@@ -8,6 +8,7 @@ The [case study](../../../../../../docs/case-studies/issue-207/README.md) descri\n - `runs/<id>.json` records job results, timestamps and the tested SHA. `runs/<id>.log.gz` is a complete available run log. `*.unavailable.txt` records the provider response when a log is inaccessible. Use `gzip -dc runs/<id>.log.gz | sed -n '1,1500p'` to read a log in sections.\n - Template recursive Git trees and the [CI path comparison](templates/ci-file-comparison.tsv) pin the inputs. The [adopted guidance](templates/CI-CD-BEST-PRACTICES.md) is the downloaded Hive Mind guide. The inventory matches identical content and similar filenames. The case study compares equivalent practices whose filenames differ.\n - `verification/` contains local verification logs. `artifacts/46062568123/` contains the failed etcd run’s member logs.\n+- [Initial Codecov report](github/pull-conversation-first-run.json), [integration installation inventory](github/codecov-installations.json) and [requested permissions](github/codecov-app.json) record the optional GitHub App advisory.\n \n | Evidence | Location |\n | --- | --- |\ndiff --git a/docs/case-studies/issue-207/README.md b/docs/case-studies/issue-207/README.md\nindex afe81bf0..f75a35da 100644\n--- a/docs/case-studies/issue-207/README.md\n+++ b/docs/case-studies/issue-207/README.md\n@@ -11,7 +11,7 @@ All times are UTC on 2026-11-27. The [evidence index](../../../dev/log/issues/20\n | 20:18–20:21 | After the C# release advanced `main` to `df8b0f8`, JS client conformance for `03f44dd` was cancelled while reopening native pages. The earlier Rust Windows test was cancelled mid-suite. Their status gates correctly rejected the cancellations. |\n | 20:29–20:30 | The replacement JS client run failed its real etcd scenario. A paused node had been resumed before the test checked that the leader changed. |\n | 20:57–21:00 | The issue update recorded the still-running Rust check. The generated initial commit of draft #208 added a root `.gitkeep`, and required JavaScript failed the layout guard. The failure propagated to dependent jobs. |\n-| After 21:00 | The Rust release advanced `main` to `d8a26c9`. The next server workflow again reported HTTP 404 for the same package. The PR branch incorporated the new default-branch tip before the fixes. |\n+| After 21:00 | The Rust release advanced `main` to `d8a26c9`. The next server workflow again reported HTTP 404 for the same package. JS client conformance on the same main revision succeeded in both journal modes, confirming that the earlier leader assertion failed intermittently. The PR branch incorporated the new default-branch tip before the fixes. |\n \n ## Requirements and verification\n \n@@ -49,6 +49,7 @@ All times are UTC on 2026-11-27. The [evidence index](../../../dev/log/issues/20\n \n - **Node FFI and LLVM branch coverage.** Node labels the direct `node:ffi` backend experimental. `cargo-llvm-cov` similarly reports the experimental LLVM branch mode on stable. The real FFI backend and branch coverage remain enabled. Switching to native Node-API bindings or dropping branch coverage would change the packaging or verification contract. The workflows preserve those lifecycle messages. [Node v26 FFI](https://nodejs.org/docs/latest-v26.x/api/ffi.html) · [cargo-llvm-cov](https://github.com/taiki-e/cargo-llvm-cov)\n - **Codecov and Dependabot.** Codecov’s PGP verification prints the key trust-database advisory alongside a good signature and verified checksum. Dependabot’s managed environment rehashes a bundled CA file and reports that it contains several certificates. The relevant upload and managed jobs completed. [Codecov wrapper](https://github.com/codecov/wrapper) · [OpenSSL rehash](https://docs.openssl.org/3.5/man1/openssl-rehash/)\n+- **Codecov GitHub integration.** The coverage comment on PR #208 reported full coverage of modified coverable lines and asked for the Codecov GitHub App. The organization installation list contained no Codecov entry. Installation grants the integration write access to checks, status and pull requests and needs an organization owner’s approval. The existing coverage uploads and coverage checks run independently of that installation. [Codecov report](https://github.com/link-foundation/link-cli/pull/208#issuecomment-7228504998) · [Codecov GitHub App](https://github.com/apps/codecov)\n - **Concurrency tooling.** GitHub job concurrency is sufficient for repository writers. A local action or custom lock service would not protect jobs pending on independent runners. The pinned Actionlint release still treats the documented queue property as unknown. The exception matches that diagnostic only and policy tests enforce its allowed placement and value. [GitHub concurrency](https://docs.github.com/en/actions/how-tos/write-workflows/choose-when-workflows-run/control-workflow-concurrency) · [Actionlint #657](https://github.com/rhysd/actionlint/issues/657)\n - **Election observation.** The etcd v3 maintenance endpoint already supplies member, leader and term. Polling it while the original process is stopped provides direct evidence without a new client dependency or an arbitrary election sleep. [etcd maintenance API](https://etcd.io/docs/v3.6/dev-guide/api_reference_v3/#service-maintenance-etcdserveretcdserverpb-rpc-proto)\n \n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
