[2026-11-27T23:17:05.334Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1105","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,320p' .github/workflows/security.yml && git diff origin/main...HEAD -- .github/workflows/security.yml\"","aggregated_output":"name: Security\n\n# Mirrors the security workflow shared by the C#, Rust and JS\n# ai-driven-development-pipeline templates, merged into a single file because\n# this repository ships all three languages (issue #96).\n\non:\n  push:\n    branches: [main]\n  pull_request:\n    types: [opened, synchronize, reopened]\n  schedule:\n    - cron: '0 6 * * 1'\n  workflow_dispatch:\n\n# Least-privilege default; jobs escalate individually when needed.\npermissions:\n  contents: read\n\n# Provide Git config to actions/checkout itself; checkout runs git init before\n# any workflow step can configure Git, which otherwise prints the\n# default-branch hint into every log.\nenv:\n  GIT_CONFIG_COUNT: '1'\n  GIT_CONFIG_KEY_0: ini…nch\n  GIT_CONFIG_VALUE_0: main\n\njobs:\n  # === STAGE GATE (issue #111) ===\n  # Jobs that install Rust or .NET wait for the JavaScript stage (lint,\n  # `npm run test:js`, parity check) of the same commit; a failed, cancelled\n  # or skipped stage leaves them skipped.\n  javascript:\n    name: javascript\n    uses: ./.github/workflows/javascript-stage.yml\n\n  codeql:\n    name: CodeQL (${{ matrix.language }})\n    needs: [javascript]\n    # Cached overlay-base SARIF retains extraction diagnostics from the base\n    # even after the PR repairs the source (confirmed in run 42133108866).\n    # A full database makes the completeness gate describe this checkout.\n    env:\n      CODEQL_OVERLAY_DATABASE_MODE: none\n      # The compare API truncates at 300 files and warns on evidence-heavy PRs.\n      # Run the complete queries directly, alongside the full extraction above.\n      CODEQL_ACTION_DIFF_INFORMED_QUERIES: 'false'\n    runs-on: ubuntu-24.04\n    timeout-minutes: 30\n    concurrency:\n      group: check-${{ github.workflow }}-${{ github.event_name == 'pull_request' && github.event.action == 'synchronize' && github.ref || github.event_name == 'push' && github.sha || github.run_id }}-codeql-${{ matrix.language }}\n      cancel-in-progress: ${{ github.event_name == 'pull_request' && github.event.action == 'synchronize' }}\n    permissions:\n      actions: read\n      contents: read\n      security-events: write\n    strategy:\n      fail-fast: false\n      # build-mode has to be declared per language. Leaving it unset made every\n      # run log \"Cannot build an overlay database because build-mode is set to\n      # 'undefined'\" and fall back to a full database, and drove the standalone\n      # autobuild step, whose inputs the action now reports as DEPRECATED\n      # (issue #96). C# used `autobuild`, which still logged \"Cannot build an\n      # overlay-base database because build-mode is set to \"autobuild\" instead\n      # of \"none\"\" on every run (issue #134); buildless extraction is supported\n      # for C#, so every language is now analysed from source.\n      matrix:\n        include:\n          - language: csharp\n            build-mode: none\n          - language: rust\n            build-mode: none\n          - language: javascript-typescript\n            build-mode: none\n          - language: python\n            build-mode: none\n          - language: actions\n            build-mode: none\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v7\n        with:\n          persist-credentials: false\n\n      # Buildless C# extraction still restores NuGet packages to resolve\n      # dependency types, so the SDK stays.\n      - name: Setup .NET\n        if: matrix.language == 'csharp'\n        uses: actions/setup-dotnet@v6\n        with:\n          dotnet-version: '10.0.403' # Exact version uses the public builds feed; channel redirect returns HTTP 409.\n\n      # With build-mode set here the action builds the database itself, so the\n      # deprecated github/codeql-action/autobuild step is no longer needed.\n      - name: Initialize CodeQL\n        uses: github/codeql-action/init@v4\n        with:\n          languages: ${{ matrix.language }}\n          build-mode: ${{ matrix.build-mode }}\n          config-file: ./.github/codeql/codeql-config.yml\n          # Opt in when an upload/extraction fails without useful diagnostics.\n          debug: ${{ vars.CI_VERBOSE == 'true' }}\n\n      - name: Analyze\n        uses: github/codeql-action/analyze@v4\n        with:\n          output: codeql-results\n\n      - uses: actions/setup-node@v7\n        with:\n          node-version: '26.x'\n\n      - name: Require complete analysis without unresolved findings\n        run: node .github/scripts/check-codeql-results.mjs codeql-results\n\n      - name: Preserve SARIF for investigation\n        if: ${{ !cancelled() }}\n        uses: actions/upload-artifact@v7\n        with:\n          name: codeql-${{ matrix.language }}\n          path: codeql-results/**/*.sarif\n          if-no-files-found: error\n\n  dependency-review:\n    name: Dependency Review\n    if: github.event_name == 'pull_request'\n    runs-on: ubuntu-24.04\n    timeout-minutes: 10\n    concurrency:\n      group: check-${{ github.workflow }}-${{ github.event_name == 'pull_request' && github.event.action == 'synchronize' && github.ref || github.event_name == 'push' && github.sha || github.run_id }}-dependency-review\n      cancel-in-progress: ${{ github.event_name == 'pull_request' && github.event.action == 'synchronize' }}\n    permissions:\n      contents: read\n      pull-requests: write\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v7\n        with:\n          persist-credentials: false\n\n      - name: Review dependency changes\n        uses: actions/dependency-review-action@v5\n        with:\n          fail-on-severity: high\n          comment-summary-in-pr: on-failure\n\n  cargo-audit:\n    name: Cargo audit (${{ matrix.manifest }})\n    needs: [javascript]\n    runs-on: ubuntu-24.04\n    timeout-minutes: 10\n    concurrency:\n      group: check-${{ github.workflow }}-${{ github.event_name == 'pull_request' && github.event.action == 'synchronize' && github.ref || github.event_name == 'push' && github.sha || github.run_id }}-cargo-audit-${{ matrix.manifest }}\n      cancel-in-progress: ${{ github.event_name == 'pull_request' && github.event.action == 'synchronize' }}\n    strategy:\n      fail-fast: false\n      matrix:\n        manifest: [rust, rust/wasm, docs/case-studies/issue-100/evidence/external-range/rust]\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v7\n        with:\n          persist-credentials: false\n\n      - uses: taiki-e/install-action@073e1fd0bc889c9aee68dbaaa927cde1b5653a83 # v2.90.11\n        with:\n          tool: cargo-audit@0.23.0\n\n      # `unmaintained`, `unsound` and `yanked` advisories are warnings, and a\n      # warning does not move `cargo audit`'s exit status: it prints\n      # \"warning: N allowed warnings found\" and exits 0, so the job passed while\n      # showing findings (issue #134). Ported from the\n      # rust-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template.\n      - name: Audit committed Cargo.lock\n        env:\n          MANIFEST: ${{ matrix.manifest }}\n        run: cargo audit --file \"$MANIFEST/Cargo.lock\" --deny warnings\n\n  npm-audit:\n    strategy:\n      fail-fast: false\n      matrix:\n        directory: [js, js/client, js/server]\n    name: Audit npm lock (${{ matrix.directory }})\n    runs-on: ubuntu-24.04\n    timeout-minutes: 10\n    concurrency:\n      group: check-${{ github.workflow }}-${{ github.event_name == 'pull_request' && github.event.action == 'synchronize' && github.ref || github.event_name == 'push' && github.sha || github.run_id }}-npm-audit-${{ matrix.directory }}\n      cancel-in-progress: ${{ github.event_name == 'pull_request' && github.event.action == 'synchronize' }}\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v7\n        with:\n          persist-credentials: false\n\n      - uses: actions/setup-node@v7\n        with:\n          node-version: '26.x'\n\n      - name: Audit current lock\n        working-directory: ${{ matrix.directory }}\n        run: npm audit --package-lock-only --audit-level=high\n\n  nuget-audit:\n    name: Audit every NuGet dependency graph\n    needs: [javascript]\n    runs-on: ubuntu-24.04\n    timeout-minutes: 15\n    concurrency:\n      group: check-${{ github.workflow }}-${{ github.event_name == 'pull_request' && github.event.action == 'synchronize' && github.ref || github.event_name == 'push' && github.sha || github.run_id }}-nuget-audit\n      cancel-in-progress: ${{ github.event_name == 'pull_request' && github.event.action == 'synchronize' }}\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v7\n        with:\n          persist-credentials: false\n      - uses: actions/setup-dotnet@v6\n        with:\n          dotnet-version: '10.0.403' # Exact version uses the public builds feed; channel redirect returns HTTP 409.\n      - uses: actions/setup-node@v7\n        with:\n          node-version: '26.x'\n      - name: Audit direct and transitive packages and validate the complete result\n        run: node .github/scripts/audit-nuget-dependencies.mjs\n      - name: Preserve dependency graphs and diagnostics\n        if: ${{ !cancelled() }}\n        uses: actions/upload-artifact@v7\n        with:\n          name: nuget-audit\n          path: artifacts/security\n          if-no-files-found: error\n\n  python-audit:\n    name: Audit resolved Python CI tools\n    runs-on: ubuntu-24.04\n    timeout-minutes: 10\n    concurrency:\n      group: check-${{ github.workflow }}-${{ github.event_name == 'pull_request' && github.event.action == 'synchronize' && github.ref || github.event_name == 'push' && github.sha || github.run_id }}-python-audit\n      cancel-in-progress: ${{ github.event_name == 'pull_request' && github.event.action == 'synchronize' }}\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v7\n        with:\n          persist-credentials: false\n      - uses: actions/setup-python@v7\n        with:\n          python-version: '3.14'\n      - name: Audit pinned tools and their resolved dependencies\n        run: pipx run pip-audit==2.10.1 --strict --requirement .github/scripts/requirements-quality.txt\n\n  # === COMMITTED SECRETS ===\n  # CodeQL and the audit jobs look at code and dependencies; nothing looked at\n  # the literal contents of the tree. This repository commits CI evidence under\n  # dev/log, which is exactly where a token pasted from a workflow log would end\n  # up unnoticed (issue #96). Ported from the pipeline templates' secrets-scan\n  # job. Git inventories tracked files, including force-added logs/experiments;\n  # build-output ignores must never hide committed evidence from this scan.\n  secrets-scan:\n    name: Scan for committed secrets\n    runs-on: ubuntu-24.04\n    timeout-minutes: 10\n    concurrency:\n      group: check-${{ github.workflow }}-${{ github.event_name == 'pull_request' && github.event.action == 'synchronize' && github.ref || github.event_name == 'push' && github.sha || github.run_id }}-secrets-scan\n      cancel-in-progress: ${{ github.event_name == 'pull_request' && github.event.action == 'synchronize' }}\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v7\n        with:\n          persist-credentials: false\n\n      - uses: actions/setup-node@v7\n        with:\n          node-version: '26.x'\n\n      - name: Install locked secret scanner\n        run: npm ci --prefix js --ignore-scripts\n      - name: Run secretlint on every tracked file\n        run: node .github/scripts/check-secrets.mjs\n      - name: Verify ignored-log regression\n        run: node experiments/issue-165/reproduce-ignored-secret.mjs\n\n  pipeline-status:\n    name: Pipeline Status (security)\n    needs:\n      - javascript\n      - codeql\n      - dependency-review\n      - cargo-audit\n      - npm-audit\n      - nuget-audit\n      - python-audit\n      - secrets-scan\n    if: ${{ !cancelled() }}\n    runs-on: ubuntu-24.04\n    timeout-minutes: 5\n    concurrency:\n      group: check-${{ github.workflow }}-${{ github.event_name == 'pull_request' && github.event.action == 'synchronize' && github.ref || github.event_name == 'push' && github.sha || github.run_id }}-pipeline-status\n      cancel-in-progress: ${{ github.event_name == 'pull_request' && github.event.action == 'synchronize' }}\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v7\n        with:\n          persist-credentials: false\n      - uses: actions/setup-node@v7\n        with:\n          node-version: '26.x'\n      - name: Check every prerequisite\n        working-directory: .\n        env:\n          NEEDS_JSON: ${{ toJSON(needs) }}\n        run: node .github/scripts/pipeline-status.mjs\ndiff --git a/.github/workflows/security.yml b/.github/workflows/security.yml\nindex f82495ab..172ff8ba 100644\n--- a/.github/workflows/security.yml\n+++ b/.github/workflows/security.yml\n@@ -48,8 +48,8 @@ jobs:\n     runs-on: ubuntu-24.04\n     timeout-minutes: 30\n     concurrency:\n-      group: check-${{ github.workflow }}-${{ github.ref }}-codeql-${{ matrix.language }}\n-      cancel-in-progress: true\n+      group: check-${{ github.workflow }}-${{ github.event_name == 'pull_request' && github.event.action == 'synchronize' && github.ref || github.event_name == 'push' && github.sha || github.run_id }}-codeql-${{ matrix.language }}\n+      cancel-in-progress: ${{ github.event_name == 'pull_request' && github.event.action == 'synchronize' }}\n     permissions:\n       actions: read\n       contents: read\n@@ -126,8 +126,8 @@ jobs:\n     runs-on: ubuntu-24.04\n     timeout-minutes: 10\n     concurrency:\n-      group: check-${{ github.workflow }}-${{ github.ref }}-dependency-review\n-      cancel-in-progress: true\n+      group: check-${{ github.workflow }}-${{ github.event_name == 'pull_request' && github.event.action == 'synchronize' && github.ref || github.event_name == 'push' && github.sha || github.run_id }}-dependency-review\n+      cancel-in-progress: ${{ github.event_name == 'pull_request' && github.event.action == 'synchronize' }}\n     permissions:\n       contents: read\n       pull-requests: write\n@@ -148,8 +148,8 @@ jobs:\n     runs-on: ubuntu-24.04\n     timeout-minutes: 10\n     concurrency:\n-      group: check-${{ github.workflow }}-${{ github.ref }}-cargo-audit-${{ matrix.manifest }}\n-      cancel-in-progress: true\n+      group: check-${{ github.workflow }}-${{ github.event_name == 'pull_request' && github.event.action == 'synchronize' && github.ref || github.event_name == 'push' && github.sha || github.run_id }}-cargo-audit-${{ matrix.manifest }}\n+      cancel-in-progress: ${{ github.event_name == 'pull_request' && github.event.action == 'synchronize' }}\n     strategy:\n       fail-fast: false\n       matrix:\n@@ -182,8 +182,8 @@ jobs:\n     runs-on: ubuntu-24.04\n     timeout-minutes: 10\n     concurrency:\n-      group: check-${{ github.workflow }}-${{ github.ref }}-npm-audit-${{ matrix.directory }}\n-      cancel-in-progress: true\n+      group: check-${{ github.workflow }}-${{ github.event_name == 'pull_request' && github.event.action == 'synchronize' && github.ref || github.event_name == 'push' && github.sha || github.run_id }}-npm-audit-${{ matrix.directory }}\n+      cancel-in-progress: ${{ github.event_name == 'pull_request' && github.event.action == 'synchronize' }}\n     steps:\n       - uses: actions/checkout@v7\n         with:\n@@ -203,8 +203,8 @@ jobs:\n     runs-on: ubuntu-24.04\n     timeout-minutes: 15\n     concurrency:\n-      group: check-${{ github.workflow }}-${{ github.ref }}-nuget-audit\n-      cancel-in-progress: true\n+      group: check-${{ github.workflow }}-${{ github.event_name == 'pull_request' && github.event.action == 'synchronize' && github.ref || github.event_name == 'push' && github.sha || github.run_id }}-nuget-audit\n+      cancel-in-progress: ${{ github.event_name ==