[2026-11-27T23:18:56.304Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1113","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n 'Block|block|Windows|CodeQL|14|Security' docs/case-studies/issue-207/README.md dev/log/issues/207/pulls/208/README.md /tmp/link-cli-207-pr-body.md\"","aggregated_output":"docs/case-studies/issue-207/README.md:11:| 20:18–20:21 | After the C# release advanced `main` to `df8b0f8`, JS client conformance for `03f44dd` was cancelled while reopening native pages. The earlier Rust Windows test was cancelled mid-suite. Their status gates correctly rejected the cancellations. |\ndocs/case-studies/issue-207/README.md:16:| 21:38–21:40 | The hosted conformance job passed the corrected real etcd scenario in both journal modes and uploaded the member logs. [Conformance job](https://github.com/link-foundation/link-cli/actions/runs/46069793278/job/140744356887) |\ndocs/case-studies/issue-207/README.md:17:| 21:53 | The Windows Rust suite and release jobs finished on `d8a26c9`. The JS server registry preflight remained the only failed workflow on that main revision. [Rust pipeline](https://github.com/link-foundation/link-cli/actions/runs/46067149253) · [Server preflight](https://github.com/link-foundation/link-cli/actions/runs/46067149214) |\ndocs/case-studies/issue-207/README.md:18:| 22:11 | All 14 workflows passed on the first PR revision, `b2c74235`. Windows Rust passed the full suite, golden receipt check and native LSM example runs within its existing budget. [Rust pipeline](https://github.com/link-foundation/link-cli/actions/runs/46069793342) |\ndocs/case-studies/issue-207/README.md:19:| 22:20 | While testing `e4ababbb`, Windows IPC exited after JavaScript received `EPERM` deleting a mapped ring during stream teardown. The same matrix passed on `b2c74235` and the latest main revision. [Failed job](https://github.com/link-foundation/link-cli/actions/runs/46075606690/job/140762688754) |\ndocs/case-studies/issue-207/README.md:32:| Keep cross-language IPC checks reliable | Windows may deny deletion while a native peer still maps a ring region. JavaScript now leaves that deletion for the last endpoint to close, matching the native implementations and the protocol. Early deletion, other filesystem errors and the original handshake rejection are covered by the focused tests. The JS client version advances to `0.5.1`. |\ndocs/case-studies/issue-207/README.md:35:| Deliver one PR with evidence and release verification | [PR #208](https://github.com/link-foundation/link-cli/pull/208) owns this work. Issue #207 had no required sub-issues or blocking-issue links when its timeline was captured. npm server release remains dependent on maintainer setup. |\ndocs/case-studies/issue-207/README.md:47:| Audit workflow and dependencies | Templates combine CodeQL, Actionlint, zizmor, lockfiles and secret scans, with tool-specific differences. link-cli already lints embedded shell code, keeps namespace pinning rules, scans historical evidence and runs CodeQL, dependency review and package ecosystem audits. Template Actionlint workarounds use a narrow exception or preprocess supported queue syntax. link-cli pairs a narrow diagnostic exception with a local queue policy check. |\ndocs/case-studies/issue-207/README.md:63:- **Windows ring ownership.** The JS descriptor closes before its deletion attempt. The native peer can retain its mapped view while it processes the hangup. Windows denies deletion of an active mapping, and Node 26.13.1 reports that permission error as `EPERM`. Both native implementations close their views before attempting removal, so the JS client returns from teardown on Windows sharing errors and lets that peer remove the file. Fixed-delay retries would keep the JS stream open and still depend on when the peer releases its view. The existing `CLINK_IPC_TRACE=1` toggle records when deletion falls to the peer. [IPC protocol](../../protocol/ipc-transports-v1.md#rendezvous-directory) · [Windows file disposition](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows-hardware/drivers/ddi/ntddk/ns-ntddk-_file_disposition_information_ex#remarks) · [Node 26.13.1 removal](https://github.com/nodejs/node/blob/v26.13.1/src/node_file.cc#L1895-L1925)\ndev/log/issues/207/pulls/208/README.md:5:- [Original issue](github/issue.json), [comments](github/issue-comments.json), [timeline](github/issue-timeline.json), [sub-issues](github/issue-sub-issues.json) and [blockers](github/issue-blocked-by.json).\ndev/log/issues/207/pulls/208/README.md:17:| Rust Windows test cancelled mid-suite | `runs/46059980682.log.gz`, lines 14386 and 25007 |\ndev/log/issues/207/pulls/208/README.md:19:| Real etcd passed the revised paused-leader scenario in both journal modes | `runs/46069793278.log.gz`, lines 10651 and 10670. [Hosted conformance job](https://github.com/link-foundation/link-cli/actions/runs/46069793278/job/140744356887) |\ndev/log/issues/207/pulls/208/README.md:20:| Windows Rust unit tests completed in 1,228.20 seconds on the first PR revision | `runs/46069793342.log.gz`, line 35760. [Hosted Windows job](https://github.com/link-foundation/link-cli/actions/runs/46069793342/job/140747171857) |\ndev/log/issues/207/pulls/208/README.md:21:| Windows IPC returned `EPERM` in `RingStream._destroy` while closing a mapped ring | [Failed job log](github/46075606690.failed.log#L119), lines 119–138. [Reproduced before](verification/windows-ring-before.log), [passing after](verification/windows-ring-after.log), [focused IPC suite](verification/windows-ring-ipc-tests.log), [complete client coverage](verification/windows-ring-client-coverage.log.gz) and [Linux interop](verification/windows-ring-interop-linux.log) |\n/tmp/link-cli-207-pr-body.md:8:- Fix Windows `mmap` and `file` ring teardown. A peer can still hold the mapping after JavaScript closes its descriptor. Both endpoints attempt removal after closing their regions, and JavaScript defers the sharing error to the peer. Bump the JS client to `0.5.1`.\n/tmp/link-cli-207-pr-body.md:16:- Windows IPC reproduced the mapped-file `EPERM`. Run `node --test --test-name-pattern='Windows ring cleanup' js/client/test/ipc-ring.test.mjs` to exercise shutdown, a handshake rejection and other I/O errors. The hosted IPC matrix also runs cross-language mmap and file conversations on Windows. [Original failure](https://github.com/link-foundation/link-cli/actions/runs/46075606690/job/140762688754)\n/tmp/link-cli-207-pr-body.md:18:- Hosted etcd passed the revised scenario in both journal modes. The anonymous package check downloaded `@link-foundation/link-cli-client@0.5.0` and reproduced npm HTTP 404 for `@link-foundation/link-cli-server@0.1.1`. [Hosted conformance](https://github.com/link-foundation/link-cli/actions/runs/46069793278/job/140744356887)\n/tmp/link-cli-207-pr-body.md:24:The npm server package is absent from the public registry, and its OIDC exchange returns HTTP 404. An npm scope maintainer needs to publish the first public version or make an existing private package public, configure GitHub trusted publishing for `link-foundation/link-cli` and `js-server.yml`, and run JS server CI on `main` with **Verify npm trusted publishing** enabled before retrying the main workflow. The PR’s tarball and code checks run independently. The real publishing criterion remains open until the maintainer steps and main verification succeed. [Failed preflight](https://github.com/link-foundation/link-cli/actions/runs/46067149214)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
