[2026-11-27T23:20:52.785Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1165","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,130p' docs/case-studies/issue-138/PHASE-POOL-PLAN.md; sed -n '1,140p' csharp/Foundation.Data.Doublets.Cli.Library/TransactionsDecorator.VersionReplay.cs; sed -n '420,515p' csharp/Foundation.Data.Doublets.Cli.Library/TransactionsDecorator.cs; rg -n 'FileShare.Delete|Directory.Move' /tmp/link-cli-207-research | head -20; git log origin/main -10 --oneline\"","aggregated_output":"# Finite supervision under shared worker starvation\n\nObjective: investigate the actual Linux C# failure on 89fbfad without widening\nany idle or suite deadline. Preserve malformed-progress rejection, diagnostics,\nactual exit codes, unconditional reaping and directory ownership.\n\n- [x] Match run 40479397432 to commit 89fbfad and its timestamp. Preserve the\n      complete log under experiments/issue-138/ci-logs. Lines 26217–26283 show\n      the finite progress control timing out despite phase 5 and exit 0.\n- [x] Trace every capture, timer, process-exit and cleanup continuation. The\n      caller-context correction is present; shared worker admission remains.\n- [x] Reproduce the observed symptom in an isolated process with a finite\n      occupied worker pool. Bound child work, memory, waits and diagnostics;\n      reap every child. Establish evidence before changing the helper.\n- [x] Add a durable regression that leaves the test runner's pool untouched.\n- [x] Correct the proven scheduling dependency, retain strict finite progress\n      validation and add independent stalled/invalid-output controls.\n- [x] Run all C# tests in Debug and Release, repository checks and coverage;\n      preserve exact commands, denominators, before/after logs and limits.\n- [ ] Publish the atomic correction and verify all fresh exact-head workflows.\n\nThe CI log does not establish the runner's precise scheduler state. Any isolated\ncontrol proves a helper dependency only. This work does not certify database\npersistence or close the outstanding R1–R12 requirements.\n\nThe isolated linked-helper control first reproduces phase 5 / exit 0 /\nTimeoutException against unchanged 89fbfad. Calling WaitForExit from the\ncontrol's main thread initially hid the race by synchronously raising the exit\nevent; the actual reproducer waits for a finite completion marker instead.\nAll three durable occupied-worker cases (progress, stall, repeated progress)\nfirst fail because supervision requires that worker. The correction gives\nprocess observation and each pipe its own dedicated finite task, checks idle\nadmission against a monotonic clock, and caps diagnostic capture at 64 KiB per\nstream. All 17 focused controls pass, including a manually advanced clock and\ncaller-context deferral. No idle or suite bound was increased. Three dedicated\nthreads per active probe are a test-only resource cost, with every task joined\nbefore the helper returns.\n\nThe complete Debug and Release suites each pass 2,451 tests with no failures or\nskips. All 221 repository checks, formatting, declarations, dependency freshness\nand workflow checks pass. The complete production coverage denominators remain\nvisible in dev/log/issues/138/pulls/139/phase-pool.txt; they remain below the\nrequested 100 percent. Fresh published-head CI is still required.\n\nPublished 950bcb3 passes eight workflows. Linux/macOS pass all 2,451 C# tests;\nthe actual Windows log also passes the original finite-progress case and all\nthree occupied-worker controls. Its one failure is a different compound setup\noperation in VersionProcessExitTests. phase-pool-ci-after.txt preserves the\nfull SHA, timestamps, every workflow and actual error lines. Continue under\nVERSION-SETUP-PROGRESS-PLAN.md without widening any idle/suite bound.\nusing System.Numerics;\n\nnamespace Foundation.Data.Doublets.Cli;\n\npublic partial class TransactionsDecorator<TLinkAddress> where TLinkAddress : IUnsignedNumber<TLinkAddress>\n{\n    private bool _versionReplay;\n    private Action? _versionReplayRecovery;\n\n    internal void RetainVersionReplayRecovery(Action recovery)\n    {\n        lock (_lock)\n        {\n            RequireVersionReplayLocked();\n            _versionReplayRecovery = recovery;\n        }\n    }\n\n    internal void ResumeVersionReplayRecovery()\n    {\n        // Only failed constructors register callbacks: their owner cannot be\n        // reached by another caller, so this lock cannot invert a live facade.\n        lock (_lock) { _versionReplayRecovery?.Invoke(); }\n    }\n\n    private void EnsureNoVersionReplayLocked()\n    {\n        if (_versionReplay)\n            throw new InvalidOperationException(\"Complete version movement before accessing transaction writes or persistence.\");\n    }\n\n    internal void BeginVersionReplay()\n    {\n        lock (_lock)\n        {\n            EnsureRecoveryCompleteLocked();\n            if (_current is not null)\n                throw new InvalidOperationException(\"A transaction still owns the data store.\");\n            _versionReplay = true;\n            // Inline writes already contain every committed effect. Establish\n            // their applied markers before movement changes those rows. Queued\n            // checkpoints subsequently observe these markers and need no redo.\n            _flushData();\n            foreach (var transition in _log)\n                if (_committed.Contains(transition.TransactionId)) MarkApplied(transition);\n            _flushLog();\n        }\n    }\n\n    internal void ReplayVersionTransition(JournalRecord<TLinkAddress> transition, bool undo)\n    {\n        lock (_lock)\n        {\n            RequireVersionReplayLocked();\n            if (undo) TryRevertRecord(transition);\n            else TryApplyRecord(transition);\n        }\n    }\n\n    internal void FlushVersionReplay()\n    {\n        lock (_lock)\n        {\n            RequireVersionReplayLocked();\n            _flushData();\n            _flushLog();\n        }\n    }\n\n    internal void FinishVersionReplay()\n    {\n        lock (_lock) { _versionReplay = false; _versionReplayRecovery = null; }\n    }\n\n    private void RequireVersionReplayLocked()\n    {\n        if (!_versionReplay) throw new InvalidOperationException(\"Version movement does not own replay.\");\n    }\n}\n    public virtual TLinkAddress SetName(TLinkAddress link, string name)\n    {\n        lock (_lock)\n        {\n            return WriteNameLocked(link, name);\n        }\n    }\n    public virtual TLinkAddress GetByName(string name) => _inner.GetByName(name);\n    public virtual void RemoveName(TLinkAddress link)\n    {\n        lock (_lock)\n        {\n            WriteNameLocked(link, null);\n        }\n    }\n\n    // Disposal --------------------------------------------------------------\n\n    /// <summary>\n    /// Stops the background worker. The wrapped data store and log store\n    /// are not disposed here; callers are expected to own those.\n    /// </summary>\n    public void Dispose()\n    {\n        Dispose(true);\n        GC.SuppressFinalize(this);\n    }\n\n    /// <summary>\n    /// Stops the background worker. Derived decorators that own extra\n    /// resources override this and call <c>base.Dispose(disposing)</c>.\n    /// </summary>\n    protected virtual void Dispose(bool disposing)\n    {\n        if (disposing)\n        {\n            Shutdown();\n        }\n    }\n\n    /// <summary>\n    /// Stops and joins the background worker before borrowed stores may close.\n    /// Concurrent callers all wait for completion. Queued checkpoint work may\n    /// be cancelled; committed journal records remain recoverable on reopen.\n    /// Callers must finish foreground operations first and callbacks must return.\n    /// </summary>\n    /// <exception cref=\"InvalidOperationException\">\n    /// Called from active background work or while holding the storage lock.\n    /// Such a caller cannot wait for worker completion without risking deadlock.\n    /// </exception>\n    public virtual void Shutdown()\n    {\n        // Check before the shutdown mutex: an external caller may already hold\n        // it while waiting for this callback (or its Task.Run descendant).\n        var work = _backgroundWork.Value;\n        if ((work is not null && Volatile.Read(ref work.Active) != 0) || Monitor.IsEntered(_lock))\n        {\n            throw new InvalidOperationException(\"Shutdown must run outside active storage callbacks.\");\n        }\n        lock (_shutdownLock)\n        {\n            if (_disposed) return;\n            lock (_lock) { EnsureNoVersionReplayLocked(); }\n            _asyncQueue.Writer.TryComplete();\n            // A single-shot CLI drains its batched checkpoint before exit.\n            // Reopening a successful import then has no per-record recovery work.\n            if (!BatchCheckpoints) _backgroundCts.Cancel();\n            // A timed join cannot establish that borrowed mappings are unused.\n            // Never hold the storage lock while waiting for its current owner.\n            _backgroundWorker.GetAwaiter().GetResult();\n            while (_asyncQueue.Reader.TryRead(out _)) { }\n            _backgroundCts.Dispose();\n            _disposed = true;\n        }\n    }\n\n    private void TryRevertTransition(Transition<TLinkAddress> transition)\n    {\n        try\n        {\n            if (transition.Before.Index == TLinkAddress.Zero)\n            {\n                DeleteIfExists(transition.After.Index);\n            }\n            else\n            {\n                RestoreLink(transition.Before);\n            }\n        }\n        catch (Exception ex)\n        {\n            Trace($\"Failed to revert transition seq={transition.Sequence}: {ex.Message}\");\n            throw;\n        }\n    }\n\nd8a26c91 chore: release rust-v3.3.1\ndf8b0f81 chore(csharp): release v5.4.1\n03f44dd5 Merge pull request #205 from link-foundation/issue-199-66734c86cf0e\n63f8fa3d Cover rollback of embedded trigger registration\n0b3ef9b5 Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/main' into issue-199-66734c86cf0e\nd87ee87c Batch transactional CLI imports and queries\ne189b22e Merge pull request #206 from link-foundation/issue-204-275f00bced2e\n5abab34b Remove generated root placeholder\n33539874 fix(deps): update ESLint and unblock the dependency audit\n301e298f Initial commit with task details\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
