 renamed within the same directory. That is, the rename operation changes the name of the file but not its location.\r\n140-\r\n141-* A fully qualified file name. (The **RootDirectory** member is NULL.) In this case, the rename operation changes the name and location of the file.\r\n142-\r\n143:* A relative file name. In this case, the **RootDirectory** member contains a handle to the target directory for the rename operation. The file name itself must be a simple file name.\r\n144-\r\n145-General rules for rename operations:\r\n146-\r\n147:* A file or directory can only be renamed within a volume. In other words, a rename operation cannot cause a file or directory to be moved to a different volume.\r\n148-\r\n149:* A volume's root directory cannot be renamed.\r\n150-\r\n151-* If **ReplaceIfExists** is set to FALSE, and the target exists, the rename operation will fail.\r\n152-\r\n153:* Even if **ReplaceIfExists** is set to TRUE, the rename operation will still fail if a file with the same name already exists and is a directory, a read-only file, or a currently executing file.\r\n154-\r\n155-* A volume's files and directories cannot be renamed if the volume is a read-only volume, such as a CDFS volume or a read-only NTFS volume.\r\n156-\r\n157:Special rules for renaming open files:\r\n158-\r\n159:* A file cannot be renamed if it has any open handles, unless it is only open because of a batch opportunistic lock (oplock) and the batch oplock can be broken immediately.\r\n160-\r\n161:* A file cannot be renamed if a file with the same name exists and has open handles (except in the batch-oplock case described earlier).\r\n162-\r\n163:* A directory cannot be renamed if it or any of its subdirectories contains a file that has open handles (except in the batch-oplock case described earlier).\r\n164-\r\n165-Special rules for renaming NTFS data streams:\r\n166-\r\n167:* The default directory stream cannot be renamed.\r\n168-\r\n169-* The new name for the stream must begin with a colon (:).\r\n170-\r\n171-* A data stream can only be renamed *within* the same file. In other words, a rename operation cannot cause a data stream to be moved to a different file.\r\n172-\r\n173:* A data stream on a directory cannot be renamed to the default data stream.\r\n174-\r\n175-* If **ReplaceIfExists** is set to TRUE, the rename operation will succeed only if a stream with the same name does not exist or is a zero-length data stream.\r\n176-\r\n177-* \"Renaming\" the default data stream is allowed, but this is not a true rename, because it leaves behind a zero-length default data stream.\r\n178-\r\n179-The size of the **FileInformation** buffer passed to [**ZwSetInformationFile**](nf-ntifs-ntsetinformationfile.md) or [**FltSetInformationFile**](../fltkernel/nf-fltkernel-fltsetinformationfile.md) must be >= **sizeof**(FILE_RENAME_INFORMATION) plus the size in bytes of the **FileName** string.\r\n180-\r\n181-## -see-also\r\n182-\r\n183-[**FltSetInformationFile**](../fltkernel/nf-fltkernel-fltsetinformationfile.md)\r\n184-\r\n185-[**IRP_MJ_SET_INFORMATION**](/windows-hardware/drivers/ifs/irp-mj-set-information)\r\n186-\r\n187-[**ZwSetInformationFile**](nf-ntifs-ntsetinformationfile.md)\r\n201:            : this(ValidateArgsAndOpenPath(path, bufferSize), encoding, detectEncodingFromByteOrderMarks, bufferSize, leaveOpen: false)\n202-        {\n203-        }\n204-\n205-        public StreamReader(string path, FileStreamOptions options)\n206-            : this(path, Encoding.UTF8, true, options)\n207-        {\n208-        }\n209-\n210-        public StreamReader(string path, Encoding? encoding, bool detectEncodingFromByteOrderMarks, FileStreamOptions options)\n211:            : this(ValidateArgsAndOpenPath(path, options), encoding, detectEncodingFromByteOrderMarks, DefaultBufferSize)\n212-        {\n213-        }\n214-\n215:        private static FileStream ValidateArgsAndOpenPath(string path, FileStreamOptions options)\n216-        {\n217-            ArgumentException.ThrowIfNullOrEmpty(path);\n218-            ArgumentNullException.ThrowIfNull(options);\n219-            if ((options.Access & FileAccess.Read) == 0)\n220-            {\n221-                throw new ArgumentException(SR.Argument_StreamNotReadable, nameof(options));\n222-            }\n223-\n224-            return new FileStream(path, options);\n225-        }\n226-\n227:        private static FileStream ValidateArgsAndOpenPath(string path, int bufferSize)\n228-        {\n229-            ArgumentException.ThrowIfNullOrEmpty(path);\n230-            ArgumentOutOfRangeException.ThrowIfNegativeOrZero(bufferSize);\n231-\n232-            return new FileStream(path, FileMode.Open, FileAccess.Read, FileShare.Read, DefaultFileStreamBufferSize);\n233-        }\n234-\n235-        public override void Close()\n236-        {\n237-            Dispose(true);\n238-        }\n239-\n# Local mirror of the cheap CI gates, so the same defects fail on `git commit`\n# instead of ten minutes into a workflow run. Ported from the AI driven\n# development pipeline templates for issue #96 and adapted to this monorepo:\n# every hook has to point at the stack-specific manifest, because the three\n# projects live under csharp/, rust/ and js/.\n#\n# Install once with:\n#   pip install pre-commit && pre-commit install\nrepos:\n  - repo: https://github.com/pre-commit/pre-commit-hooks\n    rev: v5.0.0\n    # Preserve verbatim investigation inputs, including large compressed logs.\n    # The separate secrets hook still checks all tracked evidence.\n    exclude: ^(dev/log/|docs/case-studies/)\n    hooks:\n      - id: trailing-whitespace\n      - id: end-of-file-fixer\n      - id: check-yaml\n      - id: check-json\n      - id: check-toml\n      - id: check-xml\n      - id: check-merge-conflict\n      - id: check-added-large-files\n\n  - repo: local\n    hooks:\n      # Mirrors the \"Lint and Format Check\" job of rust.yml.\n      - id: cargo-fmt\n        name: cargo fmt\n        entry: cargo fmt --manifest-path rust/Cargo.toml --all --\n        language: system\n        types: [rust]\n        pass_filenames: false\n\n      - id: cargo-clippy\n        name: cargo clippy\n        entry: cargo clippy --manifest-path rust/Cargo.toml --all-targets --all-features -- -D warnings\n        language: system\n        types: [rust]\n        pass_filenames: false\n\n      # Mirrors the \"Lint and Format Check\" job of csharp.yml. The solution sets\n      # TreatWarningsAsErrors in csharp/Directory.Build.props, so a plain build\n      # is already the warning gate.\n      - id: dotnet-format\n        name: dotnet format\n        entry: dotnet format csharp --verify-no-changes\n        language: system\n        types: [c#]\n        pass_filenames: false\n\n      # Mirrors the workflow policy and repository layout guards. These are pure\n      # Node with no dependencies, so they are fast enough for every commit.\n      - id: workflow-policy\n        name: workflow policy and repository layout tests\n        entry: node --test .github/scripts/*.test.mjs js/test/*.test.mjs csharp/scripts/*.test.mjs\n        language: system\n        files: ^(\\.github/|js/|csharp/|rust/|\\.lycheeignore|README\\.md)\n        pass_filenames: false\n\n      - id: javascript-quality\n        name: JavaScript lint and formatting\n        entry: node .github/scripts/check-javascript-quality.mjs\n        language: system\n        files: \\.(js|mjs|cjs|jsx)$\n        exclude: ^(dev/log/|docs/case-studies/)\n        pass_filenames: false\n\n      - id: secrets\n        name: secrets in tracked files including ignored evidence\n        entry: node .github/scripts/check-secrets.mjs\n        language: system\n        pass_filenames: false\n\n      - id: python-quality\n        name: Python lint, formatting and CI helper types\n        entry: python .github/scripts/check-python-quality.py\n        language: python\n        additional_dependencies: [ruff==0.17.4, mypy==2.4.1]\n        types: [python]\n        exclude: ^(dev/log/|docs/case-studies/)\n        pass_filenames: false\ncsharp/Foundation.Data.Doublets.Cli.Tests/bin/Debug/net10.0/Foundation.Data.Doublets.Cli.Tests.dll\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
