[2026-11-28T01:04:35.804Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"set -euo pipefail\nsed -n '1,58p' /tmp/link-cli-207-pr-body.md\nprintf '\\\\nLatest branch refs\\\\n'\ngit ls-remote origin refs/heads/main refs/heads/issue-207-ac4b1e2ba1ef\"","aggregated_output":"Fixes #207\n\n## Changes\n\n- Keep read-only checks for each default-branch revision and independent dispatch. Replace only superseded PR synchronization checks. Queue repository release writers so a later publish cannot displace a pending one.\n- Remove the generated root `.gitkeep`. Preserve required status checks, language stage order, and golden fixture receipts.\n- Verify the replacement etcd leader while the original member is paused. After it rejoins, verify convergence, refusal of the stale transaction, and a linearizable read through the resumed member. Set `ETCD_TEST_VERBOSE=1` or dispatch JS Client CI with **Record etcd election status and member debug logs** to capture election evidence.\n- Fix Windows `mmap` and `file` ring teardown. A peer can still hold the mapping after JavaScript closes its descriptor. Both endpoints attempt removal after closing their regions, and JavaScript defers the sharing error to the peer. Bump the JS client to `0.5.1`.\n- Retry Windows PID-lock sharing errors during cleanup in C#, Rust and JS. Bump the JS server to `0.1.2`. The C# recovery cases now share one real interrupted-store image and recover independent copies. Each fault and its deadline remain covered. Set `LINK_CSHARP_RECOVERY_TRACE=1` or the `CI_VERBOSE` repository variable for phase timings.\n- Validate both npm tarballs and their size against the JS template’s budget on pull requests and checks-only dispatches. Main publishing requires a successful trusted-publisher preflight. A separate read-only job downloads the exact published version anonymously. Registry diagnostics distinguish package setup from a lookup outage.\n- Cover shared stage inputs and integration examples in JS package triggers. Enforce a 30-minute workflow job timeout ceiling with documented caps for longer suites and release jobs. Resolve the Rust and C# source-size warnings. Combine the C# release notes into one patch changeset and correct the contributor instructions to match the validation gate.\n\n## Reproduce and verify\n\n- Draft #208 at `26852bd` fails `node --test js/test/repositoryLayout.test.mjs`. This test passes after removal of the placeholder.\n- The original run reproduces the etcd failure. JS Client CI runs the real cluster in both journal modes. Run `node --test experiments/issue-138/etcd-harness.test.mjs` for the focused election checks. [Original failure](https://github.com/link-foundation/link-cli/actions/runs/46062568123)\n- Windows IPC reproduced the mapped-file `EPERM`. Run `node --test --test-name-pattern='Windows ring cleanup' js/client/test/ipc-ring.test.mjs` to exercise shutdown, a handshake rejection and other I/O errors. The hosted IPC matrix also runs cross-language mmap and file conversations on Windows. [Original failure](https://github.com/link-foundation/link-cli/actions/runs/46075606690/job/140762688754) · [Passing Windows interop](https://github.com/link-foundation/link-cli/actions/runs/46087946769/job/140801968204)\n- The hosted Windows C# log shows one leftover PID entry after eight successful imports and one deadline in version restart recovery. The PID cleanup tests cover transient and permanent errors. The Windows C# regression opens the owner file, observes a real rename rejection, closes the handle, and verifies the retry. The restart suite still exercises all twelve injected faults. [Original Windows failures](https://github.com/link-foundation/link-cli/actions/runs/46080072295/job/140778322490)\n- Overlapping `main` revisions cancelled conformance and Rust tests. Run the CI governance and workflow policy tests in `.github/scripts` to exercise the policy. [Client cancellation](https://github.com/link-foundation/link-cli/actions/runs/46059980457) · [Rust cancellation](https://github.com/link-foundation/link-cli/actions/runs/46059980682)\n- Hosted etcd passed the revised scenario in both journal modes on `27d93ed1`. [Final conformance job](https://github.com/link-foundation/link-cli/actions/runs/46087946742/job/140802229410)\n- The anonymous package check downloaded `@link-foundation/link-cli-client@0.5.0` and reproduced npm HTTP 404 for the server at versions `0.1.1` and `0.1.2`. [Registry evidence](https://github.com/link-foundation/link-cli/blob/issue-207-ac4b1e2ba1ef/dev/log/issues/207/pulls/208/README.md)\n- Run `npm --prefix js run lint`, `npm --prefix js run test:js`, `node parity/check-parity.mjs --base origin/main`, and `npm pack --dry-run --json | node ../../.github/scripts/check-npm-tarball-size.mjs` from each npm package directory.\n- The changeset validator rejected two C# fragments on `9089b247`. Run `node csharp/scripts/validate-changeset.mjs` with the PR base and head supplied as `GITHUB_BASE_SHA` and `GITHUB_HEAD_SHA`. The corrected head passes the same gate with one patch entry. [Original gate failure](https://github.com/link-foundation/link-cli/actions/runs/46084377374/job/140791049963)\n- Local verification passed 439 JavaScript stage tests, 41 focused JS store-lock tests with full module coverage, 61 targeted C# lock and restart cases, and the Rust store-lock checks. The hosted Windows job passed all 3,567 C# tests and loaded all 41 golden fixtures. The real rename test observed Windows error `0x80070005` and succeeded after the reader closed. All twelve restart faults passed, including `intent-delete-after` in 535 ms. [Windows C# test log](https://github.com/link-foundation/link-cli/actions/runs/46087946978/job/140803337507)\n- This environment has no installed pre-commit hooks. The relevant checks were run manually, including workflow policy, JavaScript and Python quality, secrets, Rust formatting and lint, .NET formatting on the CI SDK, Actionlint and zizmor.\n\n## External verification still needed\n\nThe server package’s public metadata and exact tarball return HTTP 404 at version `0.1.2`. The real OIDC exchange also returned HTTP 404 on `main`. An npm scope maintainer needs to publish the first public version or make an existing private package public, configure GitHub trusted publishing for `link-foundation/link-cli` and `js-server.yml`, and run JS server CI on `main` with **Verify npm trusted publishing** enabled before retrying the main workflow. The PR’s tarball and code checks run independently. The real publishing criterion remains open until the maintainer steps and main verification succeed. [Failed preflight](https://github.com/link-foundation/link-cli/actions/runs/46067149214)\n\nGitHub reports a neutral PR CodeQL comparison for the C# autobuild category retired on October 24. The Security workflow scans all five current categories on both `main` and this PR. Clearing the neutral comparison requires repository-owner approval to remove the retired historical configuration from `main`. [CodeQL comparison](https://github.com/link-foundation/link-cli/runs/140802951857) · [GitHub configuration cleanup](https://docs.github.com/en/code-security/how-tos/manage-security-alerts/manage-code-scanning-alerts/resolve-alerts#removing-stale-configurations-and-alerts-from-a-branch)\n\n## Evidence and upstream reports\n\n- [Investigation, timeline and requirements](https://github.com/link-foundation/link-cli/blob/issue-207-ac4b1e2ba1ef/docs/case-studies/issue-207/README.md)\n- [Run logs, template file comparison and local verification](https://github.com/link-foundation/link-cli/blob/issue-207-ac4b1e2ba1ef/dev/log/issues/207/pulls/208/README.md)\n- [Rust template #275](https://github.com/link-foundation/rust-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template/issues/275), [JS template #325](https://github.com/link-foundation/js-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template/issues/325), [C# template #121]